WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿0

00:00:30.479 --> 00:00:34.216
<i>♪ Sincerely ♪</i>


00:00:35.017 --> 00:00:40.222
<i>♪ Oh, yes, sincerely ♪</i>


00:00:41.223 --> 00:00:45.161
<i>♪ 'Cause I love you so dearly ♪</i>


00:00:47.262 --> 00:00:51.467
<i>♪ Please say you'll be mine ♪</i>


00:00:55.237 --> 00:00:58.741
<i>♪ Sincerely ♪</i>


00:00:59.975 --> 00:01:02.145
<i>♪ Oh, you know ♪</i>


00:01:02.178 --> 00:01:06.015
<i>♪ How I love you ♪</i>


00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:10.253
<i>♪ I'll do anything for you ♪</i>


00:01:12.123 --> 00:01:16.326
<i>♪ Please say you'll be mine ♪</i>


00:01:20.197 --> 00:01:24.768
<i>♪ Oh, Lord
Won't you tell me ♪</i>


00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:30.974
<i>♪ Why I love that girlie so ♪</i>


00:02:04.642 --> 00:02:06.178
Are you looking for something?


00:02:06.211 --> 00:02:08.379
No, I'm just
doing a little shopping.


00:02:08.412 --> 00:02:10.781
We also have shoes
in the basement.


00:02:13.218 --> 00:02:15.287
Do your other customers
know that too?


00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:16.954
Mama.


00:02:16.987 --> 00:02:19.023
Which one do you like better?


00:02:19.056 --> 00:02:20.056
Pardon me.


00:02:24.395 --> 00:02:26.565
I think I like this one.


00:02:26.598 --> 00:02:29.101
Will you really need a wallet
while you're down there?


00:02:29.135 --> 00:02:31.002
Oh, Mama. Please?


00:02:33.206 --> 00:02:34.240
Okay. Fine.


00:02:34.273 --> 00:02:36.074
Let's just go pay for it
and go home now.


00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:02.500
<i>Sing out.</i>


00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:04.270
<i>♪ I love Bosco ♪</i>


00:03:04.303 --> 00:03:05.871
<i>♪ It's rich and chocolaty ♪</i>


00:03:05.904 --> 00:03:09.675
<i>♪ Chocolate-flavored Bosco
Is mighty good for me ♪</i>


00:03:09.709 --> 00:03:13.213
<i>♪ Mama puts it in my milk
for extra energy ♪</i>


00:03:13.247 --> 00:03:16.682
<i>♪ Bosco gives me iron
and sunshine vitamin D ♪</i>


00:03:16.716 --> 00:03:20.354
<i>♪ Oh, I love Bosco
That's the drink for me ♪</i>


00:03:20.386 --> 00:03:22.889
Whoa! My man!


00:03:22.922 --> 00:03:23.723
You did that.


00:03:23.756 --> 00:03:25.791
You didn't stutter,
not one time.


00:03:26.792 --> 00:03:27.693
Now, Bo, you know


00:03:27.727 --> 00:03:29.595
it's time for you to go to bed.


00:03:30.264 --> 00:03:31.797
Aw...


00:03:31.831 --> 00:03:34.167
You know you got
a big day tomorrow.


00:03:34.201 --> 00:03:35.801
Come on. Give Grandma a hug.


00:03:41.275 --> 00:03:42.475
I'll see you when you get back.


00:03:42.508 --> 00:03:43.709
Bring it in.


00:03:46.545 --> 00:03:47.513
Good night, Mr. G.


00:03:47.546 --> 00:03:48.749
All right.


00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:50.984
Oh.


00:03:51.018 --> 00:03:53.520
You two don't get married
before I get back.


00:03:53.553 --> 00:03:55.455
Can't get married
without my best man.


00:03:55.956 --> 00:03:57.125
Good night.


00:03:59.893 --> 00:04:01.428
What?
Is it my bedtime too?


00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.298
Could be.


00:04:05.999 --> 00:04:07.034
Good night.


00:04:08.169 --> 00:04:10.437
I'll call you
after Bo gets on the train.


00:04:12.373 --> 00:04:13.640
Mrs. Spearman.


00:04:14.808 --> 00:04:16.076
She'll see you tomorrow.


00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.811
- All right. Good night.
- Good night.


00:04:23.318 --> 00:04:24.785
What's wrong, Mamie?


00:04:29.457 --> 00:04:31.459
We've never been apart
this long.


00:04:33.262 --> 00:04:35.863
He's just going
to see his cousins.


00:04:35.897 --> 00:04:38.233
It's not a bad thing for him
to know where he come from.


00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.535
Well, Chicago is all
he needs to know.


00:04:40.568 --> 00:04:42.503
I don't want him seeing himself


00:04:42.537 --> 00:04:44.806
the way those people
are seen down there.


00:04:46.074 --> 00:04:47.542
Those people like me?


00:04:49.777 --> 00:04:52.013
Even you left Mississippi, Mama.


00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:57.552
Mamie, Bo is growing up.


00:04:58.354 --> 00:05:00.222
You gonna have to let him go.


00:05:02.157 --> 00:05:04.592
All right, I know that face.


00:05:04.625 --> 00:05:05.827
That is the face of


00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.330
"Mama, mind your business,
and go home."


00:05:08.364 --> 00:05:09.398
Where's my pocket book?


00:05:09.431 --> 00:05:10.632
Mm-hmm. Right here.


00:05:10.666 --> 00:05:11.800
Oh, there it is.


00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:15.472
You need to get you
some rest too.


00:05:15.504 --> 00:05:16.805
- I will.
- Come on, baby.


00:05:16.839 --> 00:05:18.841
- I'll call you tomorrow.
- All right.


00:05:23.912 --> 00:05:26.182
- Good night, Mama.
- Good night, darlin'.


00:06:12.329 --> 00:06:13.330
<i>A delightful day</i>


00:06:13.364 --> 00:06:14.498
<i>here in our town of Chicago</i>


00:06:14.532 --> 00:06:15.808
<i>and I presume
that you're, sort of,</i>


00:06:15.832 --> 00:06:17.134
<i>munching on Wrigley's Spearmint,</i>


00:06:17.168 --> 00:06:18.135
<i>and you're all relaxed,</i>


00:06:18.169 --> 00:06:20.137
<i>and pleasantly situated
wherever you are.</i>


00:06:20.171 --> 00:06:21.539
<i>The sun's probably shining</i>


00:06:21.571 --> 00:06:23.474
<i>in your heart and your town too.</i>


00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:35.554
<i>♪ There was a guy
who had some brand new tricks ♪</i>


00:06:35.586 --> 00:06:37.755
<i>♪ Played his horn
with some crazy licks ♪</i>


00:06:37.788 --> 00:06:40.425
<i>♪ The thing that made him
such a flop ♪</i>


00:06:40.459 --> 00:06:41.959
<i>♪ Was he beeped ♪</i>


00:06:41.992 --> 00:06:44.028
<i>♪ When he should've... bopped ♪</i>


00:06:44.061 --> 00:06:46.864
<i>♪ That same old guy jumped
right up on the stand ♪</i>


00:06:46.897 --> 00:06:48.737
<i>♪ But... But he couldn't seem
to dig the band ♪</i>


00:06:50.102 --> 00:06:52.137
<i>♪ Thought he was the cream
of the crop but ♪</i>


00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:54.573
<i>♪ He beeped
when he should have bopped ♪</i>


00:06:54.605 --> 00:06:55.773
I got this ready for you.


00:06:55.806 --> 00:06:57.842
<i>♪ All the cats
would gather around ♪</i>


00:06:57.875 --> 00:06:59.910
<i>♪ To see what
he was tryin' to prove ♪</i>


00:07:00.911 --> 00:07:03.215
<i>♪ But anyone
could plainly see ♪</i>


00:07:03.248 --> 00:07:06.384
<i>♪ He was draggin' them
out of the groove ♪</i>


00:07:06.418 --> 00:07:09.554
<i>♪ At last the leader
turned around and said ♪</i>


00:07:09.588 --> 00:07:11.922
<i>♪ Listen, Pops,
you had better stop ♪</i>


00:07:11.956 --> 00:07:14.227
<i>♪ Oh, there you go
You did it again ♪</i>


00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:17.662
<i>♪ You just beeped
when you should've bopped ♪</i>


00:07:20.199 --> 00:07:23.536
All right, now,
you're gonna miss your train.


00:07:25.605 --> 00:07:28.073
Bo, when you get down there...


00:07:28.107 --> 00:07:29.741
Oh, not again, Mama.


00:07:29.774 --> 00:07:31.310
I've already
been to Mississippi.


00:07:31.344 --> 00:07:32.711
Only one time before,


00:07:32.744 --> 00:07:35.814
and you started a fight
with another little boy.


00:07:35.847 --> 00:07:38.717
He was picking on me.


00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.586
You're in the right
to stand up for yourself,


00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.321
but that's not
what I'm talking about.


00:07:46.658 --> 00:07:48.227
Well, they have
a different set of rules


00:07:48.261 --> 00:07:49.328
for Negroes down there.


00:07:49.362 --> 00:07:50.662
Are you listening?


00:07:51.464 --> 00:07:53.232
Yes.


00:07:53.266 --> 00:07:55.668
You have to be extra careful
with White people.


00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:57.970
You can't risk looking at them
the wrong way.


00:07:58.004 --> 00:07:59.005
I know.


00:08:01.208 --> 00:08:02.209
Bo.


00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.978
Be small down there.


00:08:07.481 --> 00:08:08.681
Like this?


00:08:27.033 --> 00:08:28.734
Instead of your father's ring,


00:08:28.768 --> 00:08:30.237
how about you wear the cufflinks


00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:31.538
we got you last Christmas?


00:08:31.572 --> 00:08:33.607
They'll look so handsome on you.


00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:35.677
No, Mama.


00:08:35.709 --> 00:08:37.178
I wanna wear the ring.


00:08:48.523 --> 00:08:50.724
Thank you.


00:08:51.259 --> 00:08:52.493
Go on downstairs.


00:08:52.527 --> 00:08:54.329
I need to finish
getting ready myself.


00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.255
Ah, morning, Mamie!


00:09:19.288 --> 00:09:21.390
Morning, Preacher.
Good morning, Wheeler.


00:09:21.423 --> 00:09:22.790
Hi, Miss Mamie.
Hi, Bo.


00:09:22.824 --> 00:09:24.660
You're leaving Chicago too soon.


00:09:24.693 --> 00:09:25.994
You were only here a few days.


00:09:26.027 --> 00:09:27.596
I didn't need
no more days than that.


00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.531
I got to see some family,
a few friends.


00:09:29.565 --> 00:09:30.675
Maybe we get you to come down...


00:09:30.699 --> 00:09:31.766
- see us.
- All aboard!


00:09:31.799 --> 00:09:33.144
I like it just fine out here,
Preacher.


00:09:33.168 --> 00:09:33.935
All right, now.


00:09:33.968 --> 00:09:35.671
Bo, stay close to your cousins.


00:09:35.704 --> 00:09:37.005
Preacher, you and Aunty Lizzie


00:09:37.038 --> 00:09:39.541
make sure Bo calls and writes
every chance he gets.


00:09:39.575 --> 00:09:41.143
I need to know he's okay.


00:09:41.176 --> 00:09:42.278
Don't worry.


00:09:42.311 --> 00:09:44.422
Me, Lizzie, and the boys
will have a stern eye on him.


00:09:44.446 --> 00:09:46.080
Goodbye, Mamie.


00:09:47.683 --> 00:09:49.285
All right, now.
Come on, Bobo.


00:09:49.318 --> 00:09:50.152
Buh-bye, Mama.


00:09:50.185 --> 00:09:52.421
Oh, Bo!
You didn't kiss me goodbye.


00:09:52.454 --> 00:09:53.988
Mama. I gotta go.


00:09:54.922 --> 00:09:56.090
Listen to Preacher.


00:09:56.125 --> 00:09:58.628
Stay with your cousins
at all times.


00:09:58.662 --> 00:10:00.397
Be extra careful.


00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:02.031
I already know.


00:10:05.368 --> 00:10:06.369
You know what?


00:10:07.836 --> 00:10:10.140
I won't need to keep the time
on my vacation.


00:10:10.674 --> 00:10:11.708
Wind it every day.


00:10:11.741 --> 00:10:13.376
Last call!
Train's leaving!


00:10:20.116 --> 00:10:22.185
Buh-bye, Mama.


00:10:22.218 --> 00:10:24.086
Come on, Bobo.
Aight, Mamie.


00:11:23.948 --> 00:11:25.283
Time to move now.


00:12:28.815 --> 00:12:30.183
Now,


00:12:30.216 --> 00:12:32.218
all you gotta do
is pinch the bract right here,


00:12:32.251 --> 00:12:34.554
so you don't
get your fingertips...


00:12:36.255 --> 00:12:39.292
Hey, look at the size
of that bird.


00:12:40.226 --> 00:12:41.561
Whoa!


00:12:41.594 --> 00:12:43.464
Where'd you get that ring?


00:12:43.497 --> 00:12:45.532
Oh, it was my daddy's.


00:12:45.566 --> 00:12:47.501
He died a hero in the war.


00:12:48.302 --> 00:12:50.036
Well, let me try it on.


00:12:50.938 --> 00:12:53.240
Um, maybe later.


00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:54.641
All right.


00:13:08.054 --> 00:13:09.490
- Bo?
- Is he all right?


00:13:09.989 --> 00:13:11.191
Bobo!


00:13:11.558 --> 00:13:12.559
Come on.


00:13:13.327 --> 00:13:15.094
Roar!


00:13:15.128 --> 00:13:18.030
From the depths
of an ancient tomb,


00:13:18.064 --> 00:13:20.601
echoes a sound
that shakes the world.


00:13:21.201 --> 00:13:23.705
Meet the mummy, Simmy!


00:13:23.738 --> 00:13:24.973
Stop!


00:13:25.005 --> 00:13:26.441
You gonna get us in trouble.


00:13:26.474 --> 00:13:30.578
Or better yet, fired.
I'm done picking these fields.


00:13:30.612 --> 00:13:32.747
What do y'all do
with all this cotton anyway?


00:13:33.748 --> 00:13:35.583
We sell it.


00:13:35.617 --> 00:13:38.319
Mr. Frederick, who own
the land, take his share.


00:13:38.353 --> 00:13:40.421
I go to market with our haul.


00:13:40.455 --> 00:13:43.258
- Sounds pretty square.
- Hmm.


00:13:43.291 --> 00:13:44.835
Pa, you gonna let him
sass you that way?


00:13:44.859 --> 00:13:46.093
What way?


00:13:46.127 --> 00:13:48.047
The boy doesn't know
where his clothes come from.


00:13:50.698 --> 00:13:51.599
Nah.


00:13:51.633 --> 00:13:53.868
I take it back, Bobo.
Stay off the farm.


00:13:55.537 --> 00:13:57.872
City boy won't even know
how he found a whuppin'.


00:14:36.077 --> 00:14:38.013
Yes, he is.


00:14:38.047 --> 00:14:39.515
Damn near pass out.


00:14:45.454 --> 00:14:47.657
Come on, sit down.
Sit down, come on.


00:14:52.529 --> 00:14:53.597
Hey, young boy.


00:14:55.398 --> 00:14:56.766
How you doin' there,
young fella?


00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:57.867
Come on, learn somethin'.


00:14:57.901 --> 00:14:59.245
Well, I'm about raised
from the dead


00:14:59.269 --> 00:15:00.503
by all this excitement.


00:15:02.205 --> 00:15:03.239
Pay attention here,


00:15:03.273 --> 00:15:04.874
you gonna let us
learn you something.


00:15:06.309 --> 00:15:07.477
I'll make damn sure.


00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.579
I'mma do what I do.


00:15:24.094 --> 00:15:25.428
Thank you, ma'am.


00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:37.808
You look like a movie star.


00:15:38.743 --> 00:15:39.744
What?


00:15:44.982 --> 00:15:46.183
Where's Bobo?


00:15:46.217 --> 00:15:48.085
He's in there.


00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:51.188
Simmy. See to Bobo
while he's inside.


00:15:57.862 --> 00:15:58.863
See?


00:16:10.175 --> 00:16:11.376
Come on.


00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:13.045
Bye!


00:16:13.078 --> 00:16:15.148
Buh-bye!


00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:17.182
- Come on, let's go!
- Yeah?


00:16:38.403 --> 00:16:40.605
She getting her gun.
She getting her gun, y'all.


00:16:40.639 --> 00:16:41.606
Come on! Move!


00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:42.841
- Get up, now! Come on!
- Move!


00:16:42.874 --> 00:16:45.711
Move!
She goin' to get a gun, y'all!


00:16:45.744 --> 00:16:48.313
- Get in!
- Just lay low.


00:16:48.346 --> 00:16:49.549
Come on, Mau!


00:17:57.551 --> 00:17:58.952
Why aren't you at work?


00:18:01.189 --> 00:18:02.456
Is everything okay?


00:18:04.591 --> 00:18:06.960
That trip we planned
to take Bo on?


00:18:07.361 --> 00:18:08.562
Let's go now.


00:18:10.265 --> 00:18:12.467
You wanna go right now?


00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:13.978
You said you weren't feeling
that well.


00:18:14.002 --> 00:18:16.504
I was just missing Bo.


00:18:20.608 --> 00:18:23.711
I'm still missing Bo.


00:18:23.745 --> 00:18:25.480
We have never been apart
this long,


00:18:25.513 --> 00:18:27.216
and he's gonna be gone
another week.


00:18:27.249 --> 00:18:29.118
I need to keep doing things


00:18:29.151 --> 00:18:32.453
to take my mind off
of this feelin'.


00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:36.591
Okay.


00:18:37.293 --> 00:18:39.594
I can't go right now, but, uh,


00:18:40.196 --> 00:18:41.297
we'll try in a few days.


00:18:41.329 --> 00:18:44.065
Promise me we'll go on the trip?


00:18:45.767 --> 00:18:46.768
Of course.


00:19:02.451 --> 00:19:05.288
I'm trying not to act so silly!


00:19:05.322 --> 00:19:06.755
Better watch yourself.


00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:10.260
I don't know,
'cause when he looks at me,


00:19:10.293 --> 00:19:12.329
I just lose my mind!


00:19:12.361 --> 00:19:14.697
Oh!
But just be yourself.


00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:17.900
Okay. I'll try.
It's gonna be all right.


00:19:22.471 --> 00:19:25.242
Oh! Nice try.


00:19:25.275 --> 00:19:26.742
It's a high-speed
competition, huh?


00:19:26.775 --> 00:19:28.811
They call you city boy,
or somethin'?


00:19:31.314 --> 00:19:32.948
Think you so damn funny, huh?


00:19:35.319 --> 00:19:36.620
Why you whistle like that?


00:19:37.687 --> 00:19:40.258
Look, it's been three days,
okay?


00:19:40.291 --> 00:19:41.534
And we haven't heard
nothin' more


00:19:41.558 --> 00:19:42.792
about what I did in Money.


00:19:42.826 --> 00:19:44.828
That's 'cause no one knows
your face 'round here.


00:19:44.861 --> 00:19:46.240
That don't mean
they not in one of 'em cars


00:19:46.264 --> 00:19:47.298
looking for us.


00:19:47.331 --> 00:19:48.932
Look, I said I was sorry.


00:19:50.134 --> 00:19:51.768
We gotta tell Pappa.


00:19:51.801 --> 00:19:54.171
We all agreed
we wouldn't say anything.


00:19:54.205 --> 00:19:55.705
He'll make Bobo go home.


00:19:55.739 --> 00:19:57.440
So what?


00:19:57.474 --> 00:19:59.377
You don't see what's been
going on around here?


00:19:59.409 --> 00:20:00.610
They killin' Negroes


00:20:00.644 --> 00:20:03.314
for doing way less
than what you did in Money.


00:20:03.347 --> 00:20:05.182
You ain't no White man, Bobo.
You one of us!


00:20:05.216 --> 00:20:06.449
Hey, leave him alone, Maurice.


00:20:06.483 --> 00:20:08.252
Mrs. Bryant must've kept it
to herself.


00:20:08.286 --> 00:20:09.786
No one has to know.


00:20:28.606 --> 00:20:31.343
Willie Mae, Ollie,


00:20:31.376 --> 00:20:33.878
I swear you two are losing
on purpose.


00:20:33.911 --> 00:20:35.822
Yeah, well, you must have
all the luck tonight, Mamie.


00:20:35.846 --> 00:20:37.815
Mm-hmm.


00:20:37.848 --> 00:20:39.483
Now, we've been here all night,


00:20:39.517 --> 00:20:41.819
and you still haven't told us
what's bothering you.


00:20:41.852 --> 00:20:43.288
I'm fine.


00:20:43.322 --> 00:20:45.157
I got a letter today
from Aunty Lizzie.


00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:48.360
She said Bo is really happy.
That's all I needed to hear.


00:20:48.393 --> 00:20:49.760
Mm.


00:20:49.794 --> 00:20:51.038
- That's real good, Mamie.
- -Mm-hmm.


00:20:51.062 --> 00:20:52.997
My boy, Curtis, just made it
down to Mississippi.


00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:53.898
I already told Uncle,


00:20:53.931 --> 00:20:55.633
"Make sure he see Bo
tomorrow."


00:20:55.666 --> 00:20:56.969
Bo would like that.


00:20:57.002 --> 00:20:58.103
Yeah.


00:20:58.137 --> 00:20:59.747
It'd be nice for him
to have another friend...


00:20:59.771 --> 00:21:01.807
- from the city there with him.
- -Mm-hmm.


00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.542
Oh, he just doesn't understand


00:21:03.575 --> 00:21:05.311
how different things are
down there.


00:21:05.345 --> 00:21:06.545
Yeah.


00:21:06.578 --> 00:21:09.349
Aunty Lizzie said
Bo's been working the fields.


00:21:09.382 --> 00:21:11.417
Oh!


00:21:11.451 --> 00:21:14.753
I can't imagine
Bo in the hot sun


00:21:14.786 --> 00:21:16.588
all day pulling some cotton.


00:21:16.621 --> 00:21:17.990
No.


00:21:18.023 --> 00:21:21.461
But Aunty Lizzie said I raised
one nice, hardworking boy.


00:21:21.493 --> 00:21:23.061
- That's my Bo.
- Yes.


00:21:27.499 --> 00:21:29.735
Can't believe
he's been gone a week.


00:21:30.736 --> 00:21:32.904
Gene and I wanna take
a trip soon,


00:21:32.938 --> 00:21:35.141
but I really wanna go down
to Mississippi


00:21:35.174 --> 00:21:36.641
and bring my son home.


00:21:37.577 --> 00:21:39.979
If Bo could just
get his feet back


00:21:40.013 --> 00:21:42.982
onto the Chicago soil,
he'd be one happy kid.


00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:52.759
I... I don't know
why I said that.


00:21:57.563 --> 00:21:59.199
Looks like
your little winning streak


00:21:59.233 --> 00:22:00.234
is over, Mamie.


00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:07.374
Well, look at that.


00:22:07.408 --> 00:22:08.808
You wanna play one more hand?


00:22:08.841 --> 00:22:09.642
Sure.


00:22:09.675 --> 00:22:11.178
But you deal this time.


00:22:11.211 --> 00:22:13.546
Absolutely.
You still gonna lose.


00:22:17.617 --> 00:22:19.753
These cards, girl.


00:22:20.888 --> 00:22:22.623
<i>A grand jury has declined</i>


00:22:22.656 --> 00:22:23.924
<i>to indict the suspect</i>


00:22:23.957 --> 00:22:26.194
<i>for the murder of Reverend
George Washington Lee,</i>


00:22:26.227 --> 00:22:29.531
<i>a Mississippi Negro man killed
while driving his car.</i>


00:22:29.563 --> 00:22:33.000
<i>Lee lead
the Belzoni, Mississippi NAACP</i>


00:22:33.033 --> 00:22:35.769
<i>in his efforts to register
hundreds of Negroes</i>


00:22:35.803 --> 00:22:37.338
<i>to vote for the first time.</i>


00:22:44.912 --> 00:22:47.148
Pappa, you and Mama
ain't asleep?


00:22:47.182 --> 00:22:48.082
Mm.


00:22:48.115 --> 00:22:50.584
How can we sleep
when y'all ain't home yet?


00:22:50.617 --> 00:22:52.520
What'd you boys
get into tonight?


00:22:52.554 --> 00:22:54.456
Nothing much, Daddy.
Just taking Bobo around.


00:22:54.489 --> 00:22:55.823
Mm.


00:22:55.856 --> 00:22:57.459
All right. Night, Ma.
Night, Pa.


00:22:57.492 --> 00:22:58.568
- Good night.
- Night night.


00:22:58.592 --> 00:22:59.727
Good night.


00:23:02.431 --> 00:23:03.631
Bobo!


00:23:07.369 --> 00:23:08.603
We leaving early tomorrow


00:23:08.636 --> 00:23:10.705
to mail that letter out
to your mama, you hear?


00:23:11.474 --> 00:23:14.577
Okay. Good night.


00:23:14.609 --> 00:23:16.278
Good night.


00:23:16.312 --> 00:23:19.415
That was close.


00:23:19.448 --> 00:23:22.083
<i>After having
registered dozens of Negroes</i>


00:23:22.117 --> 00:23:24.386
<i>to vote
in the local runoff election.</i>


00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:26.654
<i>No charges have been made.</i>


00:24:53.511 --> 00:24:54.778
Preacher!


00:24:55.546 --> 00:24:56.813
Preacher!


00:24:57.914 --> 00:24:59.283
Who is it?


00:24:59.317 --> 00:25:00.151
It's Mr. Bryant.


00:25:00.184 --> 00:25:02.386
I wanna talk to you
about that boy.


00:25:04.922 --> 00:25:05.756
Sir?


00:25:05.790 --> 00:25:06.891
I want that boy


00:25:06.924 --> 00:25:08.993
who did the talking down
in Money.


00:25:09.661 --> 00:25:12.029
Talking, sir? What talking?


00:25:12.063 --> 00:25:13.864
Open up this door, Preacher!


00:25:16.168 --> 00:25:17.169
Bobo!


00:25:18.769 --> 00:25:21.105
You better open up
this door, Preacher!


00:25:21.139 --> 00:25:22.641
Bobo! Wake up!


00:25:23.808 --> 00:25:25.611
Leave me alone.


00:25:25.644 --> 00:25:26.678
Get up! Someone's come!


00:25:26.712 --> 00:25:28.213
You know who I'm talking about!


00:25:28.247 --> 00:25:29.281
So what?


00:25:29.314 --> 00:25:30.748
They've come for you!


00:25:30.781 --> 00:25:32.150
I don't know.


00:25:32.184 --> 00:25:33.252
Who's come?


00:25:34.620 --> 00:25:36.655
I don't know what you mean,
Mr. Bryant.


00:25:36.688 --> 00:25:38.956
You got that boy from Chicago.


00:25:59.778 --> 00:26:01.347
You that big mouth nigger?


00:26:02.315 --> 00:26:03.315
Who are you?


00:26:04.082 --> 00:26:05.485
Get your clothes on.


00:26:09.255 --> 00:26:12.292
Mr. Bryant,
you ain't got to do this.


00:26:12.325 --> 00:26:13.559
He just a young boy.


00:26:13.593 --> 00:26:14.893
Better shut them eyes.


00:26:14.926 --> 00:26:16.329
- Oh!
- Simmy!


00:26:27.241 --> 00:26:29.809
You don't need
no goddamn socks, boy.


00:26:32.146 --> 00:26:34.315
I... I don't wear shoes
without socks.


00:26:36.417 --> 00:26:37.917
Don't talk back to them!


00:26:37.950 --> 00:26:39.453
We just gonna
teach him a lesson.


00:26:39.486 --> 00:26:40.654
Stay right here, Simmy!


00:26:40.688 --> 00:26:41.789
- Please!
- Move!


00:26:41.821 --> 00:26:43.190
- Don't take him!
- Move!


00:26:43.223 --> 00:26:46.025
I'll whup him
if he's done something wrong!


00:26:46.059 --> 00:26:48.629
We'll give you money.


00:26:48.662 --> 00:26:49.763
Watch out.


00:26:49.797 --> 00:26:50.997
We don't need no money!


00:26:51.732 --> 00:26:52.666
Please!


00:26:52.700 --> 00:26:54.535
The boy ain't got good sense.


00:26:54.568 --> 00:26:55.868
He's gonna learn!


00:26:58.971 --> 00:27:00.341
But, Mr. Bryant!


00:27:03.843 --> 00:27:05.145
What'd you say to my brother?


00:27:18.693 --> 00:27:19.893
All right. Get up.


00:27:23.131 --> 00:27:24.232
Carolyn!


00:27:25.400 --> 00:27:26.568
Is this the right nigger?


00:27:32.340 --> 00:27:33.475
That's the one.


00:27:34.242 --> 00:27:35.276
All right.


00:27:37.679 --> 00:27:38.847
Get off me.


00:27:38.879 --> 00:27:40.548
Shut up, boy! Shut up.


00:27:43.218 --> 00:27:45.653
All right.


00:28:44.781 --> 00:28:46.048
Look at me, boy!


00:28:48.050 --> 00:28:49.419
Hold him down!


00:28:51.020 --> 00:28:53.088
Watch it, now!


00:28:55.057 --> 00:28:56.091
Shut your mouth!


00:28:58.093 --> 00:28:59.830
Come on. Get up! Get up!


00:28:59.863 --> 00:29:00.897
Hold him up!


00:29:49.881 --> 00:29:51.082
Hello?


00:29:57.189 --> 00:29:59.324
Get out of the way, Gene!
I gotta get to Money!


00:29:59.358 --> 00:30:00.993
Money? Money?
Mamie, what's going on?


00:30:01.025 --> 00:30:02.227
They took Bo!


00:30:02.261 --> 00:30:03.562
- Who took Bo?
- I...


00:30:03.595 --> 00:30:05.664
Preacher told me two men came
and got Bo last night.


00:30:05.697 --> 00:30:07.208
I couldn't hear anything else
after that.


00:30:07.232 --> 00:30:08.867
- I gotta find Bo!
- Mamie! Mamie! Mamie!


00:30:08.901 --> 00:30:12.004
Mamie, let's go inside,
call your mama,


00:30:12.036 --> 00:30:14.038
try and get in touch with
Preacher and Aunty Lizzie


00:30:14.071 --> 00:30:15.274
for more information, okay?


00:30:16.308 --> 00:30:18.277
Come on. Come on.


00:30:20.812 --> 00:30:23.749
We give you all the glory, Lord.


00:30:23.782 --> 00:30:25.517
- Glory to God.
- Yes.


00:30:25.551 --> 00:30:28.987
Glory to God.
Yes, Lord. Glory to God.


00:30:29.021 --> 00:30:31.055
- Yes.
- Mm-hmm.


00:30:31.088 --> 00:30:33.660
He's going to bring him
back to you, baby.


00:30:34.928 --> 00:30:36.262
Yes, ma'am.


00:30:38.831 --> 00:30:40.033
Alma.


00:30:40.065 --> 00:30:41.434
Thank you.


00:30:44.571 --> 00:30:45.572
Mamie.


00:30:47.040 --> 00:30:48.241
Alma.


00:30:49.208 --> 00:30:50.743
You weren't going to tell me?


00:30:52.145 --> 00:30:53.813
I called your wife.


00:30:56.749 --> 00:31:00.587
No matter the differences
between me and your mother,


00:31:01.154 --> 00:31:02.822
I'm still your father.


00:31:04.057 --> 00:31:05.258
Mamie,


00:31:06.559 --> 00:31:08.828
we're gonna find Bo.


00:31:08.861 --> 00:31:11.230
- Mm.
- Sit down.


00:31:11.264 --> 00:31:14.602
I brought your cousin along
to help us.


00:31:14.635 --> 00:31:18.205
Do you remember Rayfield?
Rayfield Mooty.


00:31:19.273 --> 00:31:22.309
Came by the house a lot
when you was a kid.


00:31:22.343 --> 00:31:25.045
He works with some
powerful Negro people


00:31:25.079 --> 00:31:26.847
who can help us find Bo.


00:31:28.449 --> 00:31:30.184
It's been a long time, ma'am.


00:31:30.217 --> 00:31:32.186
- Nice to see you again.
- Mm.


00:31:33.420 --> 00:31:34.421
Mamie.


00:31:35.422 --> 00:31:38.392
Oh. I'm sorry.


00:31:38.425 --> 00:31:41.695
Thank you for coming,
Mr. Mooty.


00:31:41.729 --> 00:31:43.129
I've, uh...


00:31:44.765 --> 00:31:49.470
I've been in touch
with Mr. William Huff,


00:31:49.503 --> 00:31:53.240
counsel for the NAACP chapter
here in Chicago.


00:31:53.273 --> 00:31:56.144
He wants to meet with you
first thing tomorrow morning.


00:31:56.177 --> 00:31:59.447
I've included the address
to his office.


00:32:00.415 --> 00:32:01.416
Here.


00:32:04.319 --> 00:32:05.687
He has political connections


00:32:05.720 --> 00:32:07.622
throughout the state
of Mississippi.


00:32:07.656 --> 00:32:10.125
And he's in regular contact
with Mayor Daley,


00:32:10.191 --> 00:32:12.794
Congressman Dawson,
and Governor Stratton.


00:32:14.162 --> 00:32:16.798
I do know the NAACP,


00:32:16.831 --> 00:32:20.568
and it sounds like
he knows the right people


00:32:20.602 --> 00:32:24.172
who can help me find Bo.


00:32:26.142 --> 00:32:27.942
Well, I'll meet you
in Mr. Huff's office


00:32:27.976 --> 00:32:29.644
tomorrow morning at 9:00 a.m.


00:32:31.780 --> 00:32:33.615
- Thanks, Ray.
- Mm-hmm.


00:32:33.648 --> 00:32:35.184
I will see you soon.


00:32:39.722 --> 00:32:41.757
Hey.


00:32:43.626 --> 00:32:46.529
<i>♪ At last the leader
turned around and said ♪</i>


00:32:46.562 --> 00:32:48.631
<i>♪ Listen, Pops,
you had better stop ♪</i>


00:32:48.664 --> 00:32:50.833
<i>♪ Oh, there you go,
you did it again ♪</i>


00:32:50.866 --> 00:32:54.437
<i>♪ You just beeped
when you should have bopped ♪</i>


00:33:36.046 --> 00:33:37.247
It's on your calendar,


00:33:37.280 --> 00:33:38.982
and you have the meeting
right after that.


00:33:39.015 --> 00:33:40.383
Morning!


00:33:40.417 --> 00:33:41.885
Hi, John.
How are you today?


00:34:00.172 --> 00:34:02.273
Mr. Huff,
this is Mrs. Bradley.


00:34:02.306 --> 00:34:04.509
Thank you for meeting with us,
Mr. Huff.


00:34:04.542 --> 00:34:06.444
- And Mr. Mobley.
- Yes, thank you.


00:34:06.477 --> 00:34:09.447
I have great respect
for your cousin.


00:34:09.480 --> 00:34:11.516
His work with the
United Steelworkers has helped


00:34:11.549 --> 00:34:14.285
to make it one of
the strongest Negro unions.


00:34:15.220 --> 00:34:17.421
- I didn't know that.
- Mm-hmm.


00:34:21.893 --> 00:34:22.894
Are you employed?


00:34:24.562 --> 00:34:25.763
I work for the Air Force.


00:34:25.797 --> 00:34:27.765
She's the only Negro woman
in the office.


00:34:30.401 --> 00:34:31.836
Mrs. Bradley.


00:34:33.272 --> 00:34:34.505
You two aren't married?


00:34:35.840 --> 00:34:36.874
Um...


00:34:36.908 --> 00:34:37.975
No.


00:34:38.009 --> 00:34:39.344
Not yet, anyway.


00:34:40.180 --> 00:34:41.613
Where's Emmett's father?


00:34:43.715 --> 00:34:47.352
Louis Till died overseas
about 10 years ago.


00:34:47.386 --> 00:34:48.787
Uh, during the war.


00:34:50.122 --> 00:34:51.857
And Mr. Bradley?


00:34:54.393 --> 00:34:56.528
You have a lot of questions
for me, Mr. Huff.


00:34:56.562 --> 00:34:59.531
And none of them seem to have
anything to do with my son.


00:35:05.871 --> 00:35:07.307
I've been briefed on your case.


00:35:07.339 --> 00:35:09.675
Bo is not a case.


00:35:12.644 --> 00:35:14.580
I've drafted
two telegrams to send.


00:35:14.613 --> 00:35:16.782
One to Governor White
in Mississippi.


00:35:16.815 --> 00:35:18.251
The other to Governor Stratton,


00:35:18.284 --> 00:35:19.886
here in Illinois.


00:35:19.919 --> 00:35:21.855
It's important they know
about Emmett.


00:35:22.856 --> 00:35:24.724
We're currently investigating
the murders


00:35:24.757 --> 00:35:26.793
of Lamar Smith and Reverend Lee.


00:35:26.826 --> 00:35:29.729
They did a lot of work getting
Negroes registered to vote.


00:35:29.762 --> 00:35:31.332
Because of what happened
to them,


00:35:31.364 --> 00:35:32.699
the Negro press in Mississippi


00:35:32.732 --> 00:35:35.302
started to write
about Emmett's kidnapping,


00:35:35.336 --> 00:35:37.804
but it's not creating
enough pressure needed


00:35:37.837 --> 00:35:41.007
to force them
into a state-wide search.


00:35:42.909 --> 00:35:44.477
Now, as your counsel,


00:35:44.510 --> 00:35:48.148
I'd like to utilize all of
the press here in Chicago.


00:35:48.182 --> 00:35:49.358
It's more likely
to get picked up


00:35:49.382 --> 00:35:51.218
by other cities that way.


00:35:51.252 --> 00:35:52.986
You're gonna have to talk
to reporters,


00:35:54.321 --> 00:35:55.822
speak in front of cameras.


00:35:56.522 --> 00:35:59.159
So... we like to make sure


00:35:59.193 --> 00:36:02.897
that the person who's telling
the story is in public favor.


00:36:05.333 --> 00:36:07.768
It's better that I ask you
questions now


00:36:07.801 --> 00:36:10.571
than some reporter
finding something later.


00:36:15.609 --> 00:36:16.977
The reverend and Mr. Lee,


00:36:17.011 --> 00:36:19.880
I heard they were killed
right before Bo got down there.


00:36:19.914 --> 00:36:21.149
Mamie...


00:36:21.182 --> 00:36:24.919
I know these Citizen Councils
are everywhere in Mississippi.


00:36:24.952 --> 00:36:27.054
You think they had a part
in any of it?


00:36:30.191 --> 00:36:32.360
When the message to White people


00:36:32.394 --> 00:36:36.063
is to stop Negroes
from voting or advancing,


00:36:37.232 --> 00:36:39.167
by any means short of violence,


00:36:40.567 --> 00:36:41.770
it's only a matter of time


00:36:41.803 --> 00:36:44.539
before someone doesn't
stop short of it.


00:36:46.275 --> 00:36:48.710
Let's just focus on finding Bo.


00:36:54.449 --> 00:36:56.051
Why do you call him "Bo"?


00:36:59.587 --> 00:37:01.856
When I was carrying him,


00:37:03.259 --> 00:37:05.428
my mama's friend
would bring him gifts


00:37:05.460 --> 00:37:07.762
all the time, and say,


00:37:07.796 --> 00:37:09.764
"Here's another one
for little Bobo."


00:37:11.400 --> 00:37:14.602
After he was born,
it just stuck.


00:37:18.473 --> 00:37:21.009
He was a perfect baby.


00:37:21.042 --> 00:37:25.014
Born breech, and had
his share of problems, but...


00:37:27.616 --> 00:37:31.087
he was a perfect baby.


00:37:50.740 --> 00:37:52.775
Hi, we live across the street


00:37:52.808 --> 00:37:54.810
and read about
what happened to Emmett.


00:37:54.844 --> 00:37:58.014
Everybody in the neighborhood
knows that sweet little boy.


00:38:03.887 --> 00:38:05.423
But maybe
somebody will read the paper,


00:38:05.456 --> 00:38:06.723
and they'll know Bo's ours.


00:38:06.757 --> 00:38:09.092
I don't care
what anyone thinks Bo did


00:38:09.126 --> 00:38:10.961
or did not do in that store.


00:38:10.994 --> 00:38:13.897
They took my child,
and I need him back.


00:38:16.033 --> 00:38:18.001
Hello? Mr. Huff!


00:38:18.935 --> 00:38:21.406
Yes, yes, yes. I'll get Mamie.


00:38:21.439 --> 00:38:23.006
Sounds like he has good news.


00:38:24.442 --> 00:38:25.709
Mr. Huff?


00:38:26.676 --> 00:38:28.413
He wrote back?


00:38:28.446 --> 00:38:30.281
The governor wants to talk
to Mr. Huff


00:38:30.314 --> 00:38:31.848
about what happened to Bo.


00:38:31.882 --> 00:38:32.883
Thank you.


00:38:32.916 --> 00:38:34.885
Thank you for the update,
Mr. Huff.


00:38:36.454 --> 00:38:38.922
Okay. I'll be in touch.


00:38:55.507 --> 00:38:56.941
A reporter called me.


00:38:59.944 --> 00:39:02.113
He didn't wanna
tell you himself.


00:39:07.985 --> 00:39:10.556
Bo's body was found in a river.


00:39:10.588 --> 00:39:12.890
Preacher just identified him
to the sheriff.


00:39:12.924 --> 00:39:17.595
He... He recognized the ring
Bo was wearing.


00:39:22.066 --> 00:39:24.068
I'm so sorry, Mamie.


00:39:25.670 --> 00:39:27.240
He's...


00:39:28.140 --> 00:39:29.409
He's dead.


00:40:18.192 --> 00:40:20.860
<i>This is
a breaking news bulletin.</i>


00:40:21.661 --> 00:40:22.962
<i>We interrupt this broadcast</i>


00:40:22.996 --> 00:40:24.331
<i>to report a breaking news story.</i>


00:40:24.365 --> 00:40:28.768
<i>The body of Emmett Louis Till
has been found dead</i>


00:40:28.801 --> 00:40:31.738
<i>in the Tallahatchie River
near Money, Mississippi.</i>


00:40:31.771 --> 00:40:34.175
<i>Till, a Negro boy
from Chicago, was kidnapped</i>


00:40:34.208 --> 00:40:36.709
<i>while visiting relatives
in Money, Mississippi.</i>


00:40:36.743 --> 00:40:38.179
<i>Again, that breaking news.</i>


00:40:38.212 --> 00:40:40.980
<i>The body of Emmett Louis Till
has been found in Mississippi.</i>


00:40:41.014 --> 00:40:42.583
<i>We'll have details ahead...</i>


00:40:42.616 --> 00:40:43.950
<i>and J.W. Milam</i>


00:40:43.983 --> 00:40:45.885
<i>were already in police custody</i>


00:40:45.919 --> 00:40:47.555
<i>after admitting
to the kidnapping,</i>


00:40:47.588 --> 00:40:49.790
<i>but they now face
possible indictment</i>


00:40:49.823 --> 00:40:51.359
<i>for the murder of Till.</i>


00:40:51.393 --> 00:40:56.198
<i>We have proved
by two or three witnesses</i>


00:40:56.231 --> 00:40:58.732
<i>that the body found
in Tallahatchie River</i>


00:40:58.766 --> 00:41:00.302
<i>was that of Emmett Till.</i>


00:41:00.335 --> 00:41:02.736
<i>We proved
that the body had the ring...</i>


00:41:02.770 --> 00:41:03.971
<i>this lynching</i>


00:41:04.004 --> 00:41:05.839
<i>that the state of Mississippi
has decided</i>


00:41:05.873 --> 00:41:07.775
<i>to maintain this White supremacy</i>


00:41:07.808 --> 00:41:10.278
<i>by murdering children.</i>


00:41:11.712 --> 00:41:14.081
<i>Look, it was because
he was a boy,</i>


00:41:14.114 --> 00:41:16.318
<i>that's why they went there.</i>


00:41:16.351 --> 00:41:19.554
<i>They had to prove
that they were superior.</i>


00:41:19.588 --> 00:41:21.055
<i>They had to prove it</i>


00:41:21.088 --> 00:41:25.025
<i>by taking away
a 14-year-old boy.</i>


00:41:25.059 --> 00:41:26.528
Mamie, you need
to eat something.


00:41:26.561 --> 00:41:28.829
<i>The killers of the boy
felt free to lynch him</i>


00:41:28.862 --> 00:41:30.031
<i>because there is,</i>


00:41:30.065 --> 00:41:31.234
<i>in the entire state...</i>


00:41:31.267 --> 00:41:34.303
<i>no restraining influence
of decency.</i>


00:41:35.103 --> 00:41:36.103
<i>Hate.</i>


00:41:36.738 --> 00:41:38.307
<i>It's like a virus in the blood</i>


00:41:38.341 --> 00:41:39.808
<i>of the Mississippians.</i>


00:41:39.841 --> 00:41:41.544
<i>They can't help it.</i>


00:41:41.577 --> 00:41:43.044
<i>That was Roy Wilkins...</i>


00:41:43.078 --> 00:41:45.981
<i>the executive director
of the NAACP...</i>


00:41:46.014 --> 00:41:47.316
You mind if I speak with Mamie?


00:41:47.350 --> 00:41:48.859
<i>Giving his
reaction to the recent killing</i>


00:41:48.883 --> 00:41:51.987
<i>of 14-year-old Negro boy,
Emmett Till.</i>


00:41:52.020 --> 00:41:54.089
<i>Burial preparations
by local sheriffs</i>


00:41:54.122 --> 00:41:55.757
<i>have already started being made</i>


00:41:55.790 --> 00:41:57.892
<i>in Tallahatchie County,
Mississippi,</i>


00:41:57.926 --> 00:41:59.794
<i>where Till's body was found.</i>


00:41:59.828 --> 00:42:00.895
Mamie?


00:42:00.929 --> 00:42:01.796
<i>Negro leaders are calling</i>


00:42:01.830 --> 00:42:03.232
<i>on local and federal officials</i>


00:42:03.266 --> 00:42:06.502
<i>to investigate the murder,
and to indict J.W. Milam...</i>


00:42:36.500 --> 00:42:37.500
Uh...


00:42:41.571 --> 00:42:45.041
- My sincere condolences...
- Stop.


00:42:46.510 --> 00:42:47.511
I can't.


00:42:52.115 --> 00:42:54.385
I need Bo's body sent back here.


00:42:55.986 --> 00:42:57.954
I can't have him buried
in Mississippi.


00:42:57.988 --> 00:43:00.191
Mississippi won't make
that deal with you.


00:43:00.224 --> 00:43:01.225
Then make them.


00:43:03.994 --> 00:43:07.665
I'm sure Mr. Huff
can get Mayor Daley


00:43:07.699 --> 00:43:09.567
or the governor
to talk to somebody.


00:43:11.968 --> 00:43:13.136
Those people in Mississippi


00:43:13.171 --> 00:43:15.540
are trying to dump Bo
in the ground


00:43:15.573 --> 00:43:17.542
like he's just another body.


00:43:17.575 --> 00:43:18.942
He is my baby.


00:43:21.044 --> 00:43:22.447
I need to see him.


00:43:30.854 --> 00:43:32.357
I'll speak with Mr. Huff.


00:43:32.390 --> 00:43:33.390
Thank you.


00:43:44.068 --> 00:43:46.003
You know...


00:43:48.139 --> 00:43:50.942
Mamie, you have the public's
attention right now.


00:43:53.779 --> 00:43:55.046
And, uh,


00:43:56.315 --> 00:43:58.817
it would be in
a politician's best interest


00:43:58.851 --> 00:44:00.918
to help you
during an election year.


00:44:03.955 --> 00:44:06.291
There's an opportunity in that.


00:44:12.598 --> 00:44:14.634
Uh...


00:44:14.667 --> 00:44:19.606
Some organizers and executive
members of the NAACP


00:44:19.639 --> 00:44:22.475
have been speaking
with the justice department


00:44:22.509 --> 00:44:23.843
about creating legislation


00:44:23.877 --> 00:44:26.413
that would make lynching
a federal crime.


00:44:29.182 --> 00:44:32.218
What happened to Reverend Lee
was a lynching.


00:44:33.118 --> 00:44:35.954
Lamar Smith. A lynching.


00:44:38.591 --> 00:44:39.591
- Emmett...
- I...


00:44:40.926 --> 00:44:43.128
uh...


00:44:43.897 --> 00:44:47.467
We have an opportunity


00:44:47.500 --> 00:44:51.970
to use this moment to help us
pass this legislation.


00:44:52.004 --> 00:44:54.541
Might even help you get
an indictment.


00:44:54.574 --> 00:44:55.810
Maybe even a conviction.


00:44:55.843 --> 00:44:59.280
I can't think about that
right now.


00:44:59.313 --> 00:45:02.583
I just need Bo's body
sent back here.


00:45:02.616 --> 00:45:06.353
Well, the public's paying
attention right now, Mamie.


00:45:07.621 --> 00:45:09.956
See, this doesn't just have
to be about Emmett.


00:45:09.989 --> 00:45:12.660
Mr. Mooty, my son is dead!


00:45:28.074 --> 00:45:31.712
Make sure
Mr. Huff handles this today.


00:45:37.985 --> 00:45:39.321
Yes, ma'am.


00:46:30.306 --> 00:46:34.610
Rayfield's ready to
take us to the train station.


00:46:39.415 --> 00:46:42.852
I, uh, got you a wheelchair.


00:46:42.885 --> 00:46:44.353
You know, just in case.


00:46:45.688 --> 00:46:47.256
I don't want you falling down.


00:46:54.263 --> 00:46:55.698
Preacher called again.


00:46:55.731 --> 00:46:59.369
He keeps trying
to apologize to you, Mamie.


00:47:03.273 --> 00:47:04.541
Aunty Lizzie's coming up here.


00:47:04.575 --> 00:47:07.711
He has to stay behind
to finish working the fields


00:47:07.744 --> 00:47:09.680
and talk to the prosecutor.


00:47:20.691 --> 00:47:22.793
I keep asking myself...


00:47:26.330 --> 00:47:28.165
"Why is this happening?


00:47:32.536 --> 00:47:35.305
"Why did he take my child
from me?


00:47:42.413 --> 00:47:44.716
"What am I
supposed to do now?"


00:47:54.392 --> 00:47:57.261
Yeah. I have to say goodbye
to Mama.


00:48:10.808 --> 00:48:11.809
Mama.


00:48:37.069 --> 00:48:39.238
I'm the one who told him
to go down there.


00:48:42.241 --> 00:48:44.476
I wanted him to go down there.


00:48:49.748 --> 00:48:51.417
I told him to go down.


00:48:54.620 --> 00:48:57.322
I told him to go down there.


00:49:44.839 --> 00:49:47.308
All right. Get that.


00:50:11.233 --> 00:50:12.867
Oh, my God!


00:50:14.169 --> 00:50:16.470
My boy!


00:50:16.504 --> 00:50:20.307
My boy! My only child!


00:50:20.341 --> 00:50:22.676
My only boy!


00:50:24.746 --> 00:50:28.850
Oh, my Lord!
Get him out of that box!


00:50:30.219 --> 00:50:33.222
Get him out of the box!


00:50:33.256 --> 00:50:36.658
Get him out of the box!
He can't breathe!


00:50:37.959 --> 00:50:40.729
He can't breathe. My Lord!


00:50:42.831 --> 00:50:45.801
Oh, Lord, have mercy!


00:50:46.835 --> 00:50:48.171
Help me!


00:50:50.273 --> 00:50:53.074
Oh, my God!


00:50:55.043 --> 00:50:58.413
Oh, Lord, have mercy!


00:50:59.182 --> 00:51:02.317
Show me what you want me to do.


00:51:02.350 --> 00:51:05.488
Oh, Lord, show me
what you want me to do


00:51:05.521 --> 00:51:08.157
and make me able to do it!


00:51:08.192 --> 00:51:09.992
My Lord!


00:51:21.271 --> 00:51:22.638
I need to prepare you.


00:51:27.877 --> 00:51:29.378
Remove the sheet.


00:51:39.121 --> 00:51:42.358
Oh, God.


00:51:55.539 --> 00:51:57.975
Everyone, leave us.


00:55:21.016 --> 00:55:22.385
How long will it take you


00:55:22.418 --> 00:55:24.152
to turn the body over to us?


00:55:24.187 --> 00:55:25.421
Figure out the next step.


00:55:25.455 --> 00:55:27.022
Talk to the church.


00:55:27.055 --> 00:55:30.692
Gene, can you go back
to my place


00:55:30.725 --> 00:55:33.028
and bring back
Emmett's black suit?


00:55:33.061 --> 00:55:35.630
The one he wore last Christmas.


00:55:35.664 --> 00:55:37.533
Mama can tell you
exactly where it is.


00:55:37.567 --> 00:55:39.469
And make sure
to get my black dress


00:55:39.502 --> 00:55:41.204
that Bo would approve of.


00:55:41.237 --> 00:55:42.938
And his matching tie.


00:55:44.706 --> 00:55:46.576
Emmett loved this suit.


00:55:46.608 --> 00:55:48.244
It's how he'd like to be seen.


00:55:50.011 --> 00:55:51.012
Seen?


00:55:52.348 --> 00:55:55.651
Mamie, Bo's in no kind of
shape to be seen by anybody.


00:55:55.685 --> 00:55:58.754
No, he's in just
the right shape.


00:55:58.788 --> 00:56:02.959
The whole world has to see
what happened to my son.


00:56:02.992 --> 00:56:06.563
Mrs. Bradley, can I
at least fix him up a bit?


00:56:06.597 --> 00:56:07.663
Just to make him more...


00:56:07.697 --> 00:56:10.032
No one's going to believe
what I just saw.


00:56:10.334 --> 00:56:11.167
No.


00:56:11.201 --> 00:56:14.003
They have to see it
for themselves.


00:56:42.032 --> 00:56:43.700
Ms. Bradley,
what would you like to say


00:56:43.734 --> 00:56:44.768
to the men who did this?


00:56:44.801 --> 00:56:46.371
What's that smell?


00:56:48.373 --> 00:56:52.177
That smell is my son's body.


00:56:52.210 --> 00:56:56.214
He came home to me
reeking of racial hatred.


00:56:56.247 --> 00:56:58.183
His face was bludgeoned.


00:56:58.216 --> 00:57:00.285
His teeth are gone.


00:57:00.318 --> 00:57:01.785
He was shot in the head.


00:57:02.654 --> 00:57:06.357
And now I want America
to bear witness.


00:57:10.428 --> 00:57:11.828
Come with me, please.


00:57:13.631 --> 00:57:14.666
Right here, Ms. Bradley.


00:57:14.698 --> 00:57:16.067
Ms. Bradley, right here.


00:57:16.100 --> 00:57:17.379
Do you have a
message for the perpetrators?


00:57:17.403 --> 00:57:19.405
Will there be
a service, Ms. Bradley?


00:57:22.641 --> 00:57:25.177
Gene, please come be with me.


00:57:56.308 --> 00:57:58.278
<i>News of an open-casket funeral</i>


00:57:58.311 --> 00:58:00.913
<i>for the slain
14-year-old Emmett Till</i>


00:58:00.946 --> 00:58:02.815
<i>has spread
throughout the country.</i>


00:58:02.848 --> 00:58:05.084
<i>Many people were in shock
over the brutal slaying</i>


00:58:05.117 --> 00:58:06.785
<i>and couldn't believe
something like this</i>


00:58:06.819 --> 00:58:08.388
<i>could happen to a child.</i>


00:58:08.421 --> 00:58:10.657
<i>My heart goes out
to her. I'm a mother too.</i>


00:58:10.690 --> 00:58:12.124
<i>It could be any one of us.</i>


00:58:12.157 --> 00:58:14.694
<i>The right thing is to
show America, and the world,</i>


00:58:14.728 --> 00:58:15.828
<i>exactly what happened.</i>


00:58:15.861 --> 00:58:17.162
<i>We know the boy was killed,</i>


00:58:17.197 --> 00:58:19.366
<i>but you're making a freak show
of his death.</i>


00:58:19.399 --> 00:58:20.667
<i>I think she brave.</i>


00:58:20.700 --> 00:58:22.001
<i>Can't we just grieve in peace?</i>


00:58:22.034 --> 00:58:23.836
<i>This stuff ain't
gonna stop till we see it.</i>


00:58:23.869 --> 00:58:25.238
<i>I support her.</i>


00:58:25.272 --> 00:58:27.707
<i>It is my
opinion that the guilt begins</i>


00:58:27.741 --> 00:58:29.209
<i>with Mrs. Bryant...</i>


00:58:29.242 --> 00:58:31.645
<i>and I wanna see
Mrs. Bryant punished,</i>


00:58:31.678 --> 00:58:33.179
<i>those two men punished,</i>


00:58:33.213 --> 00:58:36.383
<i>and any other persons
who were in on this thing.</i>


00:58:36.416 --> 00:58:37.384
<i>The pressure should start</i>


00:58:37.417 --> 00:58:39.620
<i>from the president
of the United States,</i>


00:58:39.654 --> 00:58:41.389
<i>all the way down to the township</i>


00:58:41.422 --> 00:58:43.023
<i>of Money, Mississippi.</i>


00:58:43.056 --> 00:58:45.058
<i>I won't rest until that happens,</i>


00:58:45.091 --> 00:58:48.329
<i>even if I have to go
to Money, Mississippi myself.</i>


00:58:48.362 --> 00:58:49.697
<i>Do you have any evidence</i>


00:58:49.730 --> 00:58:50.930
<i>bearing on this case?</i>


00:58:50.964 --> 00:58:53.833
<i>I do know that this is my son.</i>


00:59:28.035 --> 00:59:30.539
You're not just my Bo anymore.


00:59:34.909 --> 00:59:35.976
Mamie...


00:59:39.348 --> 00:59:41.015
Aunty Lizzie.


00:59:44.286 --> 00:59:47.789
Simmy and Maurice stayed back
with their daddy.


00:59:47.823 --> 00:59:49.957
It was probably too much.


00:59:53.328 --> 00:59:54.496
I'm so sorry.


00:59:57.064 --> 01:00:01.002
When those men came, I tried.


01:00:02.739 --> 01:00:05.173
We all tried.


01:00:06.809 --> 01:00:08.344
I ain't going back, Mamie.


01:00:08.910 --> 01:00:11.214
I packed my stuff up,


01:00:11.247 --> 01:00:13.282
and I'm staying here for good.


01:00:14.183 --> 01:00:16.017
Preacher and the boys
will join me.


01:00:19.589 --> 01:00:20.956
I can't look, Mamie.


01:00:29.332 --> 01:00:30.333
We have to.


01:01:14.977 --> 01:01:19.148
<i>♪ When peace like a river ♪</i>


01:01:19.183 --> 01:01:20.983
I'm sorry, Ms. Mamie.


01:01:22.887 --> 01:01:27.358
<i>♪ Attendeth my way ♪</i>


01:01:27.392 --> 01:01:29.894
Bo... Bo.


01:01:29.928 --> 01:01:36.701
<i>♪ When sorrows like sea ♪</i>


01:01:36.734 --> 01:01:42.072
<i>♪ Billows roll ♪</i>


01:01:42.105 --> 01:01:48.746
<i>♪ Whatever my lot ♪</i>


01:01:49.781 --> 01:01:56.254
<i>♪ Thou hast taught me to say ♪</i>


01:01:57.087 --> 01:02:00.925
<i>♪ It is well ♪</i>


01:02:00.959 --> 01:02:05.231
<i>♪ It is well ♪</i>


01:02:05.264 --> 01:02:10.736
<i>♪ With my soul ♪</i>


01:02:12.972 --> 01:02:16.775
<i>♪ It is well ♪</i>


01:02:16.809 --> 01:02:21.614
<i>♪ It is well ♪</i>


01:02:21.647 --> 01:02:25.618
<i>♪ With my soul ♪</i>


01:02:25.651 --> 01:02:29.922
<i>♪ With my soul ♪</i>


01:02:29.955 --> 01:02:34.527
<i>♪ It is well ♪</i>


01:02:34.560 --> 01:02:39.063
<i>♪ It is well ♪</i>


01:02:39.097 --> 01:02:46.171
<i>♪ With my soul ♪</i>


01:02:46.806 --> 01:02:50.710
<i>It is well</i>


01:02:50.744 --> 01:02:55.080
<i>It is well</i>


01:02:55.114 --> 01:02:59.019
<i>With my soul</i>


01:02:59.051 --> 01:03:03.723
<i>With my soul</i>


01:03:03.757 --> 01:03:08.461
<i>It is well</i>


01:03:08.495 --> 01:03:13.065
<i>It is well</i>


01:03:13.098 --> 01:03:20.240
<i>With my soul</i>


01:03:28.883 --> 01:03:31.117
My child is dead,


01:03:32.152 --> 01:03:34.288
and she is going to be fine.


01:03:36.891 --> 01:03:41.094
Carolyn Bryant
is going to be fine.


01:03:48.402 --> 01:03:50.037
You know,
to get a murder indictment


01:03:50.071 --> 01:03:52.807
on two White men
in Mississippi is not easy.


01:03:57.211 --> 01:04:00.648
You did that, Mamie.


01:04:05.553 --> 01:04:06.555
Now...


01:04:10.258 --> 01:04:11.827
Their defense...


01:04:14.196 --> 01:04:15.864
is going to try to create doubt


01:04:15.897 --> 01:04:18.033
about the body being Emmett's.


01:04:18.066 --> 01:04:20.268
There's no body,
there's no murder conviction,


01:04:20.302 --> 01:04:23.839
and Bryant and Milam will only
face kidnapping charges.


01:04:29.411 --> 01:04:31.680
You know your child
better than anyone.


01:04:34.916 --> 01:04:36.752
You saw the body soon after.


01:04:39.588 --> 01:04:43.959
There is no testimony
like a mother's.


01:05:22.165 --> 01:05:23.685
Aren't we going
to your mama's tonight?


01:05:27.203 --> 01:05:29.406
I need to go to Mississippi
for the trial.


01:05:30.908 --> 01:05:34.344
I can testify that it was
Bo's body found in the river.


01:05:47.858 --> 01:05:48.898
When do you want us to go?


01:05:52.229 --> 01:05:54.164
Gene, I have to go without you.


01:05:54.199 --> 01:05:56.900
- What?
- Mr. Mooty has arranged for me to meet some people


01:05:56.934 --> 01:05:58.311
-down there.
- If you're going to Mississippi,


01:05:58.335 --> 01:05:59.646
- I'm going with you.
- Mr. Huff and Mr. Mooty


01:05:59.670 --> 01:06:01.004
don't think that's a good idea,


01:06:01.038 --> 01:06:03.198
- and I agree with them.
- I don't care what they think!


01:06:05.175 --> 01:06:06.211
They keep telling us


01:06:06.243 --> 01:06:07.554
what to do
and who you can talk to.


01:06:07.578 --> 01:06:10.281
And I go along with it
because I lost Bo too.


01:06:12.350 --> 01:06:13.752
I would do anything for him.


01:06:19.290 --> 01:06:20.425
You tell me, Mamie.


01:06:21.359 --> 01:06:23.862
How is risking your life
gonna help Bo?


01:06:33.838 --> 01:06:36.508
This is what they're writing
about me down there.


01:06:36.541 --> 01:06:38.877
They're making me out to be
some kind of jezebel.


01:06:38.910 --> 01:06:40.345
Two reporters called to ask


01:06:40.378 --> 01:06:42.714
about my ex-husbands
and about you.


01:06:43.848 --> 01:06:45.450
Mr. Huff was right.


01:06:45.483 --> 01:06:47.552
I'm on trial like the people
who killed Bo.


01:06:47.585 --> 01:06:50.488
Jurors will be watching me,
and reading these stories


01:06:50.522 --> 01:06:53.292
when they decide if the men
who murdered my son go free.


01:06:53.325 --> 01:06:55.694
I have to protect my image


01:06:56.796 --> 01:06:58.964
if it can help get justice
for Bo.


01:07:02.635 --> 01:07:04.737
I should be going with you,
Mamie.


01:07:04.770 --> 01:07:08.340
I need you to be there for me
in a different way right now.


01:07:13.246 --> 01:07:14.566
You're not gonna change
your mind?


01:07:16.982 --> 01:07:17.850
You know me well enough


01:07:17.883 --> 01:07:19.952
to answer that question
for yourself.


01:07:45.879 --> 01:07:48.181
<i>Not since
the Tallahatchie River flooded</i>


01:07:48.216 --> 01:07:49.649
<i>some 20 or 30 years ago</i>


01:07:49.683 --> 01:07:53.720
<i>that the townspeople had more
to talk about than this trial.</i>


01:07:53.753 --> 01:07:57.757
<i>I can't understand
how a civilized mother</i>


01:07:57.791 --> 01:08:02.729
<i>could put a dead body of
her child on public display!</i>


01:08:02.762 --> 01:08:07.100
<i>I think that this is
a result of the NAACP</i>


01:08:07.133 --> 01:08:08.735
<i>trying to make something big...</i>


01:08:08.768 --> 01:08:10.670
<i>out of just an ordinary</i>


01:08:10.704 --> 01:08:13.039
<i>criminal affair in Mississippi.</i>


01:08:23.050 --> 01:08:24.085
You're not going.


01:08:25.052 --> 01:08:26.787
Mamie, it's too dangerous


01:08:26.821 --> 01:08:28.789
for you to go down
to Mississippi right now.


01:08:29.690 --> 01:08:31.726
I heard the sheriffs
are passing along


01:08:31.759 --> 01:08:33.761
Negro license plate numbers
to the Klan members.


01:08:33.794 --> 01:08:36.497
Mr. Huff and Mr. Mooty
already have plans


01:08:36.530 --> 01:08:38.200
for me to safely travel.


01:08:38.233 --> 01:08:40.134
I'll fly to Memphis first.


01:08:40.167 --> 01:08:42.371
And then,
some people from the NAACP


01:08:42.403 --> 01:08:44.038
are going to drive me
to Clarksdale.


01:08:44.071 --> 01:08:46.741
And then, their field
secretary will pick me up


01:08:46.774 --> 01:08:48.776
and drive me to someone's house


01:08:48.809 --> 01:08:50.444
in a place called Mound Bayou.


01:08:50.478 --> 01:08:52.413
You want to go alone?


01:08:52.446 --> 01:08:55.318
I'm trying to be strong for Bo.


01:08:55.351 --> 01:08:57.185
What are you gonna do
down there?


01:08:58.221 --> 01:08:59.855
Something you can't.


01:09:05.928 --> 01:09:09.598
If my testimony can help
in any way,


01:09:10.233 --> 01:09:11.466
I have to go.


01:09:12.501 --> 01:09:15.070
I have to be there for my child.


01:09:17.273 --> 01:09:19.007
And what about my child?


01:09:27.182 --> 01:09:28.450
I'm goin' with ya.


01:09:30.752 --> 01:09:32.988
I know this is not
what we agreed on,


01:09:33.021 --> 01:09:35.491
but it's better for me
to go down there with her


01:09:35.525 --> 01:09:37.126
than for her to be there alone.


01:09:42.665 --> 01:09:45.635
You don't have to worry.
I'mma be there with you.


01:09:46.836 --> 01:09:47.837
I promise.


01:09:49.539 --> 01:09:52.242
I don't only need you
when I'm broken, Daddy.


01:10:00.149 --> 01:10:02.819
I am goin' with you.


01:10:05.154 --> 01:10:06.155
Thank you.


01:10:08.591 --> 01:10:10.860
Mama, I know you don't agree...


01:10:10.893 --> 01:10:11.894
No.


01:10:15.199 --> 01:10:16.767
But I know you have to do it.


01:10:39.623 --> 01:10:42.993
<i>♪ One a-these mornings ♪</i>


01:10:44.496 --> 01:10:47.664
<i>♪ Soon one morning ♪</i>


01:10:49.967 --> 01:10:54.605
<i>♪ I'm gonna lay down my cross ♪</i>


01:10:54.638 --> 01:10:56.740
<i>♪ Get me a crown ♪</i>


01:10:56.774 --> 01:10:59.611
<i>Mound Bayou has been
here for over 70 years.</i>


01:11:00.812 --> 01:11:02.614
It's a all-Negro town.


01:11:04.082 --> 01:11:07.619
We run all our own businesses
and all our own schools.


01:11:08.753 --> 01:11:10.289
All the Negroes
attending the trial


01:11:10.322 --> 01:11:12.291
will be staying here.


01:11:12.324 --> 01:11:13.858
This is the safest place
for 'em.


01:11:16.395 --> 01:11:17.929
Dr. Howard
created the Regional Council


01:11:17.962 --> 01:11:20.266
for Negro Leadership
here in Mound Bayou.


01:11:20.299 --> 01:11:23.701
He's also the chief surgeon
at the Taborian Hospital.


01:11:23.735 --> 01:11:25.103
He built
a lot of businesses here,


01:11:25.136 --> 01:11:27.739
including a really successful
life insurance company.


01:11:28.407 --> 01:11:30.342
That's how I met him.


01:11:30.376 --> 01:11:32.043
He gave me my first job.


01:11:33.245 --> 01:11:38.016
<i>♪ Going home one day
and tell my story ♪</i>


01:11:38.049 --> 01:11:42.988
<i>♪ I've been coming over hills
and mountain ♪</i>


01:11:43.022 --> 01:11:47.494
<i>♪ Gonna drink from
the Christian fountain ♪</i>


01:11:47.527 --> 01:11:53.032
<i>♪ Your know all of God's sons
and daughters that morning ♪</i>


01:11:53.065 --> 01:11:56.869
<i>♪ Will drink that
ole healing water ♪</i>


01:11:56.902 --> 01:11:59.138
<i>♪ And we gonna live... ♪</i>


01:12:03.742 --> 01:12:06.513
Thank you
for driving us, Mr. Evers.


01:12:06.546 --> 01:12:08.914
Please, ma'am, call me Medgar.


01:12:11.150 --> 01:12:12.252
Mrs. Bradley?


01:12:13.919 --> 01:12:16.889
Those pictures of your son
in the magazine...


01:12:19.359 --> 01:12:20.727
changed people's lives.


01:12:22.497 --> 01:12:25.832
My wife,
she's here with our son.


01:12:27.634 --> 01:12:28.845
And we're both helping
with some of


01:12:28.869 --> 01:12:30.837
the investigation work
for the trial.


01:12:32.639 --> 01:12:33.940
Now, I promise you...


01:12:36.009 --> 01:12:37.245
we are doing everything we can


01:12:37.278 --> 01:12:39.413
to get some sort of justice
for Emmett Till.


01:12:53.760 --> 01:12:56.763
We call Dr. Howard's house
"The Black Command Center."


01:12:56.796 --> 01:12:58.466
Reporters
from all the colored press


01:12:58.499 --> 01:13:00.234
work out of here
during the trial.


01:13:00.268 --> 01:13:01.203
They also help with some of


01:13:01.236 --> 01:13:02.837
the investigation work
for the trial.


01:13:02.870 --> 01:13:05.574
And what kind of investigation
y'all are gonna be doing?


01:13:05.607 --> 01:13:06.707
We're looking for witnesses


01:13:06.741 --> 01:13:08.544
who'll be brave enough
to come to trial.


01:13:11.746 --> 01:13:14.550
- Right here.
- Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.


01:13:14.583 --> 01:13:15.950
This here is,
uh, Ms. Murdock.


01:13:15.983 --> 01:13:17.919
Ms. Bradley.


01:13:17.952 --> 01:13:19.754
Ms. Turner. Mr. Booker.


01:13:19.787 --> 01:13:21.856
Pleased to meet you, ma'am.


01:13:21.889 --> 01:13:23.592
This here is my son, Darrell.


01:13:23.625 --> 01:13:25.126
And my wife, Myrlie.


01:13:25.159 --> 01:13:27.929
It's an honor to meet you,
Mrs. Bradley.


01:13:28.430 --> 01:13:29.430
Mr. Carthan.


01:13:31.366 --> 01:13:32.366
Hey, you don't mind?


01:13:33.000 --> 01:13:35.169
Over here is Amzie Moore.


01:13:35.204 --> 01:13:36.205
He's the president


01:13:36.238 --> 01:13:38.674
of the Regional Council
for Negro Leadership.


01:13:38.706 --> 01:13:41.643
And I am Dr. Theodore Howard.


01:13:41.677 --> 01:13:45.215
Welcome to Mound Bayou,
Mrs. Bradley.


01:13:46.683 --> 01:13:48.917
- Mr. Carthan.
- Sir.


01:13:48.951 --> 01:13:52.988
Let me just say that
we are so...


01:13:54.156 --> 01:13:56.758
honored to have you
here with us.


01:13:57.660 --> 01:13:58.695
Thank you.


01:13:58.727 --> 01:13:59.928
Thank you.


01:14:01.497 --> 01:14:03.732
Now, what are you drinking?


01:14:07.035 --> 01:14:08.438
Not a lot of people would use


01:14:08.471 --> 01:14:10.306
their money the way you do.


01:14:10.340 --> 01:14:12.208
Well, we need money


01:14:12.242 --> 01:14:14.977
for the freedom fight
that we're in now.


01:14:16.346 --> 01:14:17.447
We need money...


01:14:18.747 --> 01:14:21.783
to protect Negroes who are...


01:14:22.518 --> 01:14:23.953
simply trying to exercise


01:14:23.987 --> 01:14:25.888
their constitutional right
to vote,


01:14:25.922 --> 01:14:28.726
to speak at trial.


01:14:32.061 --> 01:14:34.831
I had a really good life
in Chicago


01:14:34.864 --> 01:14:36.467
before they took Bo from me.


01:14:39.002 --> 01:14:40.537
I never thought much
about the world


01:14:40.571 --> 01:14:42.439
outside of just me and Bo,


01:14:43.674 --> 01:14:45.875
my job, my family, my friends.


01:14:50.113 --> 01:14:51.981
Mrs. Bradley,
have you thought about, um,


01:14:52.015 --> 01:14:53.783
what you're going to do
after the trial?


01:14:55.419 --> 01:14:56.953
After the trial?


01:14:56.986 --> 01:14:58.722
I'm sure you've considered


01:14:58.756 --> 01:15:00.990
continuing your work
with the NAACP.


01:15:01.024 --> 01:15:03.960
Or with our Regional Council,
right here.


01:15:03.993 --> 01:15:08.466
Your story... speaks
to the urgency of Negro rights


01:15:08.500 --> 01:15:12.437
more than anything
this country has ever heard.


01:15:12.470 --> 01:15:13.871
I've been sharing my story


01:15:13.904 --> 01:15:18.343
because I want those two men
to pay for what they did.


01:15:18.376 --> 01:15:20.077
And I do too.


01:15:20.110 --> 01:15:23.715
But I do not believe
that justice will be rendered


01:15:23.748 --> 01:15:27.385
by 12 jurors
who look exactly like


01:15:27.419 --> 01:15:31.155
the two so-called men
who are on trial.


01:15:34.626 --> 01:15:37.961
And our fight, and your story,


01:15:39.397 --> 01:15:45.303
must continue and will not end
with one single verdict.


01:15:50.509 --> 01:15:52.545
Mrs. Bradley.


01:17:06.853 --> 01:17:08.222
That's the mother!


01:17:08.922 --> 01:17:10.324
Come on, get out the way.


01:17:10.358 --> 01:17:12.460
Mrs. Bradley,
why are you here?


01:17:12.493 --> 01:17:14.094
- Ms. Bradley.
- Ms. Bradley!


01:17:14.127 --> 01:17:15.463
Come on, say something!


01:17:15.496 --> 01:17:17.063
- Will you testify?
- Come on!


01:17:17.097 --> 01:17:18.308
- You gotta give us something.
- Mrs. Bradley.


01:17:18.332 --> 01:17:19.567
Mamie?


01:17:19.600 --> 01:17:20.600
It's all right, Daddy.


01:17:23.371 --> 01:17:25.206
I am here to confirm...


01:17:28.709 --> 01:17:31.279
What's wrong with you?


01:17:32.012 --> 01:17:33.481
Let's get inside.
Come on.


01:17:46.327 --> 01:17:47.328
No.


01:18:01.543 --> 01:18:02.977
How dare you?


01:18:08.015 --> 01:18:09.284
It's all right, Mamie.


01:18:20.229 --> 01:18:21.230
Go on!


01:18:40.950 --> 01:18:42.150
Amzie.


01:18:46.088 --> 01:18:48.825
Mrs. Bradley, I'd like you
to meet Ruby Hurley.


01:18:48.858 --> 01:18:50.326
She's also a part of our team.


01:18:50.360 --> 01:18:52.896
It's truly an honor
to meet you, Mrs. Bradley.


01:18:52.929 --> 01:18:55.163
Thank you.


01:18:55.197 --> 01:18:56.575
Thank you,
it's a pleasure to meet you.


01:18:56.599 --> 01:18:57.600
My pleasure.


01:18:57.634 --> 01:18:59.010
- We'll be with you, ma'am.
- Thank you.


01:18:59.034 --> 01:19:00.202
- Right this way.
- Thank you.


01:19:00.236 --> 01:19:02.137
- Thank you.
- You're welcome, of course.


01:19:05.642 --> 01:19:06.642
Hello, niggers!


01:19:07.877 --> 01:19:09.913
I got about eight seats
down there


01:19:09.946 --> 01:19:11.782
for you
and your nigger reporters.


01:19:12.583 --> 01:19:13.717
Rest of you can stand.


01:19:14.718 --> 01:19:15.718
You Mamie?


01:19:18.622 --> 01:19:19.823
What's this?


01:19:19.857 --> 01:19:22.191
That's a damn summons.


01:19:22.226 --> 01:19:24.828
I thought you uppity niggers
could read.


01:19:24.862 --> 01:19:27.631
Mamie?
Don't let him get to you.


01:19:27.665 --> 01:19:28.665
Come on, now.


01:19:29.667 --> 01:19:31.368
Ah, there's James Hicks.


01:19:31.402 --> 01:19:33.571
We can go and sit with him
and the other reporters.


01:19:34.672 --> 01:19:36.740
Have you spoke
with the prosecution team?


01:19:36.774 --> 01:19:38.976
Only once before, on the phone.


01:19:39.009 --> 01:19:40.377
It was brief.


01:19:40.411 --> 01:19:43.013
Hopefully, this won't take
too long. Get together later.


01:19:43.047 --> 01:19:44.915
- Mr. Smith.
- Yes.


01:19:44.949 --> 01:19:46.584
Mrs. Bradley.


01:19:46.617 --> 01:19:47.617
Mamie.


01:19:52.958 --> 01:19:54.225
- Hmm.
- Come on.


01:19:56.761 --> 01:19:58.463
All rise!


01:19:58.496 --> 01:20:02.334
The Honorable Judge
Curtis Swango presiding.


01:20:04.836 --> 01:20:05.870
Please be seated.


01:20:09.841 --> 01:20:11.175
There will be no pictures taken


01:20:11.209 --> 01:20:13.278
during court proceedings.


01:20:13.311 --> 01:20:18.416
Bailiff, have the jurors
come in and take a seat.


01:20:18.450 --> 01:20:23.153
Also, get me a Coke sometime.
All right?


01:20:41.040 --> 01:20:43.009
Your Honor,
the State has just learned


01:20:43.042 --> 01:20:45.176
of the existence
of another witness


01:20:45.211 --> 01:20:47.178
to the murder of Emmett Till.


01:20:47.213 --> 01:20:49.081
The State requests a recess


01:20:49.115 --> 01:20:50.883
in order to gather the witness.


01:20:52.284 --> 01:20:53.619
Objection, Your Honor!


01:20:53.653 --> 01:20:56.856
Your Honor, this will only
delay proceedings. Come on.


01:20:56.889 --> 01:20:58.624
Hmm.


01:20:58.658 --> 01:20:59.925
Objection overruled.


01:20:59.959 --> 01:21:02.595
It seems like
a reasonable request.


01:21:03.396 --> 01:21:05.196
Thank you, Your Honor.


01:21:05.231 --> 01:21:06.766
I'll give you
till tomorrow morning


01:21:06.799 --> 01:21:08.934
to find your witness.


01:21:13.439 --> 01:21:15.542
The court will have a recess.


01:21:15.575 --> 01:21:19.112
We will resume at 9:00 a.m.
tomorrow morning.


01:21:20.847 --> 01:21:22.249
Court dismissed!


01:21:29.690 --> 01:21:32.693
Medgar, take me to Money.


01:21:35.128 --> 01:21:37.564
All right. Okay.


01:22:30.585 --> 01:22:32.453
That's where it happened?


01:22:34.789 --> 01:22:35.823
Yes, ma'am.


01:22:37.459 --> 01:22:40.829
The shop's been closed
since the day of the arrest.


01:22:45.100 --> 01:22:46.769
Most of the patrons
were Negroes.


01:25:39.478 --> 01:25:42.181
Your mama tells me
you're all moving up north


01:25:42.214 --> 01:25:43.214
after the trial.


01:25:44.784 --> 01:25:47.086
Daddy says
it's not gonna be safe.


01:25:55.528 --> 01:25:57.063
Thank you.


01:26:05.205 --> 01:26:06.540
We're sorry, ma'am.


01:26:11.979 --> 01:26:12.979
We're so sorry.


01:26:17.884 --> 01:26:20.754
You all didn't know
this was going to happen.


01:26:23.523 --> 01:26:24.791
Come here.


01:26:31.898 --> 01:26:33.066
It's okay.


01:26:34.469 --> 01:26:35.736
Hmm.


01:26:45.179 --> 01:26:46.781
Where's your daddy?


01:27:14.075 --> 01:27:15.076
You gonna sit?


01:27:19.481 --> 01:27:20.882
I saw your boys.


01:27:23.918 --> 01:27:26.021
Was probably hard for them
to see you.


01:27:32.094 --> 01:27:33.095
You gonna sit?


01:27:45.607 --> 01:27:47.709
Did you have a shotgun
in your house


01:27:47.743 --> 01:27:48.977
the night they took Bo?


01:27:52.248 --> 01:27:56.553
I've been wanting to explain
to you what happened.


01:27:56.585 --> 01:27:58.153
You told me that part.


01:27:58.187 --> 01:27:59.755
White men came knocking


01:27:59.788 --> 01:28:01.300
- on my door, Mamie.
- I know that part.


01:28:01.324 --> 01:28:02.258
They had a gun.


01:28:02.292 --> 01:28:03.926
You have a gun!


01:28:07.063 --> 01:28:10.501
How long did you
stand there doing nothing


01:28:10.534 --> 01:28:12.236
while they took my child?


01:28:12.269 --> 01:28:13.069
If I'd have shot them,


01:28:13.103 --> 01:28:15.839
they would've killed
all of mine!


01:28:15.872 --> 01:28:18.875
It'd be hunting season
for every Negro in Money!


01:28:22.346 --> 01:28:23.813
We have to live here, Mamie.


01:28:25.549 --> 01:28:26.950
Bobo was with my boys


01:28:26.983 --> 01:28:28.918
when he went to talk
to some White woman.


01:28:28.952 --> 01:28:30.363
You understand
what that mean down here?


01:28:30.387 --> 01:28:33.189
Don't you dare blame Bo
for what happened to him!


01:28:33.224 --> 01:28:35.758
I don't blame him!


01:28:46.803 --> 01:28:48.806
I had to make a choice
that night.


01:28:49.608 --> 01:28:51.909
In a moment, I had to choose.


01:28:54.346 --> 01:28:56.780
And you chose yours over mine.


01:28:56.814 --> 01:29:00.951
It wasn't just two White men
with a gun that night.


01:29:02.254 --> 01:29:06.023
It was every White man
who'd rather see a Negro dead


01:29:06.056 --> 01:29:08.759
than breathin'
the same air as him.


01:29:08.792 --> 01:29:11.695
Every sheriff,
every judge in this town


01:29:11.729 --> 01:29:13.931
was at my door that night.


01:29:13.964 --> 01:29:18.270
I was facin' a lot more
than two men with a gun.


01:29:29.047 --> 01:29:31.250
He was my only child.


01:29:42.628 --> 01:29:43.828
I know.


01:30:01.179 --> 01:30:03.349
That's why you're moving
after the trial...


01:30:05.551 --> 01:30:07.219
because you're going to testify?


01:30:11.123 --> 01:30:15.161
No Negro in Money has ever
spoken against a White man...


01:30:17.196 --> 01:30:18.398
and lived.


01:31:00.575 --> 01:31:01.709
That's the house.


01:31:01.743 --> 01:31:03.944
If he runs,
make sure he doesn't get away.


01:31:03.977 --> 01:31:05.380
Amzie, right here.


01:31:14.187 --> 01:31:15.456
Hey! Not so loud.


01:31:15.490 --> 01:31:16.557
You'll scare him off.


01:31:20.695 --> 01:31:22.095
We told you
to leave Willie alone.


01:31:22.129 --> 01:31:23.964
Let's have
a conversation inside.


01:31:23.997 --> 01:31:25.767
He didn't see nothin'!


01:31:25.799 --> 01:31:28.035
Come out or we're comin' in.


01:31:28.068 --> 01:31:30.037
You gonna get the boy killed.


01:31:33.676 --> 01:31:35.877
Hey! Hey!


01:31:40.783 --> 01:31:42.050
Come on, come on!


01:32:12.046 --> 01:32:13.148
We need to keep him here


01:32:13.182 --> 01:32:14.718
just in case he runs off again.


01:32:14.751 --> 01:32:17.086
I ain't gonna run.


01:32:17.119 --> 01:32:19.289
I'll tell 'em
what I saw that night.


01:32:19.322 --> 01:32:21.257
And what about
your grandparents?


01:32:22.057 --> 01:32:23.101
Would you say that they heard


01:32:23.125 --> 01:32:24.503
some sounds
comin' out the barn too?


01:32:24.527 --> 01:32:27.731
No, no, I promised them I was
gonna keep them out of it.


01:32:27.764 --> 01:32:29.232
We're gonna finance security


01:32:29.265 --> 01:32:31.634
for your entire family
after they testify,


01:32:31.668 --> 01:32:33.135
so don't you worry none, son.


01:32:34.371 --> 01:32:35.372
All right?


01:32:36.306 --> 01:32:38.207
<i>His name is Willie Reed,</i>


01:32:38.241 --> 01:32:40.477
<i>a field hand for
J.W.'s brother.</i>


01:32:41.678 --> 01:32:43.580
He's a witness
who lives on the farm


01:32:43.613 --> 01:32:45.415
not too far from where he saw


01:32:45.448 --> 01:32:47.283
J.W. and Roy Bryant


01:32:47.317 --> 01:32:49.486
and several other men
take Emmett.


01:32:49.519 --> 01:32:52.389
Now, Willie's family
also works for the Milams,


01:32:52.422 --> 01:32:54.958
so they also heard
a lot of noise that night.


01:32:54.991 --> 01:32:56.960
There were other men?


01:32:58.829 --> 01:33:01.197
It pains me
to have to tell you this,


01:33:01.232 --> 01:33:04.468
but there were some colored
men that were involved.


01:33:07.872 --> 01:33:10.241
Colored men did this to my boy?


01:33:10.274 --> 01:33:12.108
Well, they work
for Milam and Bryant,


01:33:12.142 --> 01:33:14.578
and found out Bryant
had 'em paid to skip town.


01:33:15.513 --> 01:33:16.514
What...


01:33:20.718 --> 01:33:23.219
I can fix that for you.


01:33:31.462 --> 01:33:34.465
It means a lot,


01:33:35.933 --> 01:33:37.235
what you're doing.


01:33:42.039 --> 01:33:43.442
Thank you.


01:33:46.411 --> 01:33:47.546
Thank you.


01:33:48.647 --> 01:33:49.980
It's the right thing to do.


01:34:00.024 --> 01:34:01.593
Go ahead and put these on.


01:34:32.558 --> 01:34:34.961
It's difficult for me
to fall asleep


01:34:34.993 --> 01:34:36.529
before Medgar gets home.


01:34:40.500 --> 01:34:41.701
I've wanted to meet you.


01:34:43.068 --> 01:34:45.203
What you did
with those photographs...


01:34:45.238 --> 01:34:48.374
What you're doin' now,
it's, um...


01:34:48.407 --> 01:34:51.109
It's nothing a mother
wouldn't do for her child.


01:34:53.646 --> 01:34:54.647
Hmm.


01:34:55.982 --> 01:34:57.584
How old's your son?


01:34:57.618 --> 01:35:00.219
Two.


01:35:02.422 --> 01:35:04.090
We almost didn't take him
and his sister


01:35:04.123 --> 01:35:06.058
with us from Jackson, but I...


01:35:07.461 --> 01:35:08.996
I'm trying to keep
the family together


01:35:09.028 --> 01:35:10.731
as much as possible these days.


01:35:14.368 --> 01:35:16.003
I'm sure you heard
about what happened


01:35:16.035 --> 01:35:18.104
to our friends Lamar Smith
and Reverend Lee.


01:35:18.137 --> 01:35:20.340
Yes, I have.


01:35:21.441 --> 01:35:23.310
Medgar and I worked closely
with 'em.


01:35:24.778 --> 01:35:26.980
We did good work.


01:35:27.014 --> 01:35:28.424
We got a lot of Negroes
registered to vote


01:35:28.448 --> 01:35:30.517
for the first time
in Mississippi,


01:35:31.818 --> 01:35:34.788
and that created the biggest
targets on our backs.


01:35:44.265 --> 01:35:46.801
I, um...


01:35:49.771 --> 01:35:53.140
I believe in the work
we're doin' for our people.


01:35:54.042 --> 01:35:55.276
I do.


01:35:58.246 --> 01:36:00.615
But I don't want my children
to have to live in fear.


01:36:02.850 --> 01:36:04.028
I have enough fear for all of us


01:36:04.052 --> 01:36:06.086
every time I wait for Medgar
to get home.


01:36:10.892 --> 01:36:12.460
Emmett just wanted
to go on vacation


01:36:12.493 --> 01:36:14.596
and have fun with his cousins.


01:36:16.431 --> 01:36:19.166
He never thought
anything would happen to him.


01:36:20.269 --> 01:36:26.207
He knew how different
things were down here,


01:36:26.241 --> 01:36:30.779
but I never raised him
to have any fear growing up.


01:36:33.114 --> 01:36:35.718
I wanted him to be a boy.


01:36:35.751 --> 01:36:38.687
And to not have his childhood
taken away from him.


01:36:41.724 --> 01:36:43.492
But it happened anyway.


01:37:03.947 --> 01:37:08.217
We do the best we can.


01:37:37.781 --> 01:37:38.848
Do you know Mr. Bryant?


01:37:42.920 --> 01:37:44.555
He owns the meat market.


01:37:44.588 --> 01:37:45.523
Hmm.


01:37:45.556 --> 01:37:47.892
Then you know Mr. Milam,
do ya?


01:37:50.928 --> 01:37:52.263
Not by name.


01:37:53.898 --> 01:37:55.633
But I know him.


01:37:55.666 --> 01:37:56.834
How do you know him?


01:37:59.470 --> 01:38:01.305
He showed up at my door,


01:38:02.707 --> 01:38:04.809
standing there
with a flashlight in one hand


01:38:04.842 --> 01:38:06.243
and a pistol in the other.


01:38:08.412 --> 01:38:10.213
And what happened next?


01:38:28.900 --> 01:38:31.770
He held my family at gunpoint.


01:38:34.072 --> 01:38:37.309
Then he dragged my nephew
from my home and drove off.


01:38:37.342 --> 01:38:39.044
Sambo!


01:38:41.947 --> 01:38:44.883
And would you


01:38:44.916 --> 01:38:49.488
Would you recognize Mr. Milam
were you to see him again?


01:39:00.966 --> 01:39:01.967
Yes, sir.


01:39:05.838 --> 01:39:07.473
I would.


01:39:19.786 --> 01:39:21.220
There he is.


01:39:26.526 --> 01:39:28.262
The State rests.


01:39:30.630 --> 01:39:32.398
The witness can leave now.


01:39:34.333 --> 01:39:36.068
The court will have a recess.


01:40:02.996 --> 01:40:04.498
What did you think you heard?


01:40:07.701 --> 01:40:10.737
I heard loud hollering and licks


01:40:11.939 --> 01:40:13.040
comin' from that shed.


01:40:14.341 --> 01:40:15.642
Sounded like a boy.


01:40:17.411 --> 01:40:18.612
I saw, uh...


01:40:21.181 --> 01:40:22.449
J.W. Milam.


01:40:23.750 --> 01:40:26.621
Saw a green truck
with a white top.


01:40:29.157 --> 01:40:30.358
As they drove off,


01:40:30.391 --> 01:40:34.095
there was, uh.
Two White men in the cab


01:40:34.128 --> 01:40:35.830
and three colored men
in the back.


01:40:37.432 --> 01:40:39.335
They was all sitting
next to a body.


01:40:39.367 --> 01:40:41.069
Are you sure
that's what you heard?


01:40:41.102 --> 01:40:42.237
Yes, sir.


01:40:42.271 --> 01:40:44.072
Huh. If that's what you heard,


01:40:44.105 --> 01:40:47.375
why not yell out,
or call "Help"?


01:40:51.446 --> 01:40:52.647
I...


01:40:55.917 --> 01:40:57.286
I...


01:40:57.319 --> 01:40:58.519
I couldn't.


01:40:59.454 --> 01:41:00.822
No further questions.


01:41:12.434 --> 01:41:13.636
You can leave now.


01:41:31.520 --> 01:41:33.822
Did you certify
that the body found


01:41:33.856 --> 01:41:35.190
was Emmett Till?


01:41:35.224 --> 01:41:36.792
No, I did not.


01:41:36.825 --> 01:41:39.228
I just said it was a dead body.


01:41:39.262 --> 01:41:42.698
You couldn't even tell if
the body was White or Black.


01:41:42.731 --> 01:41:44.066
Thank you, Sheriff Strider.


01:41:44.099 --> 01:41:45.467
You are excused.


01:41:48.672 --> 01:41:49.906
You want my honest opinion?


01:41:49.940 --> 01:41:52.442
I think the boy's mammy
and the NAACP


01:41:52.475 --> 01:41:55.011
plotted this whole thing.


01:41:55.045 --> 01:41:56.846
Thank you, Sheriff Strider.


01:41:58.448 --> 01:42:00.183
That boy's
still alive somewhere.


01:42:42.327 --> 01:42:43.594
Mamie...


01:42:46.465 --> 01:42:48.433
Did you have a son who,
in his lifetime,


01:42:48.467 --> 01:42:50.568
was known as Emmett Till?


01:42:52.036 --> 01:42:53.237
Yes, sir.


01:42:53.271 --> 01:42:55.106
How old was he?


01:42:55.139 --> 01:42:57.041
Fourteen years of age.


01:42:57.074 --> 01:42:58.943
Is his father living today?


01:42:59.478 --> 01:43:00.644
No, sir.


01:43:00.678 --> 01:43:02.947
He died in service.


01:43:02.980 --> 01:43:04.648
Oh.
Uh, when your husband,


01:43:04.682 --> 01:43:07.285
the father of Emmett Till,
was killed overseas,


01:43:07.319 --> 01:43:09.854
were his belongings sent to you?


01:43:09.887 --> 01:43:10.956
Yes, sir.


01:43:12.557 --> 01:43:14.092
I now hand you


01:43:15.294 --> 01:43:18.331
a ring that has engraved on it,


01:43:18.364 --> 01:43:22.502
May 25th, 1943,


01:43:22.534 --> 01:43:24.002
with the large initials L.T.


01:43:24.036 --> 01:43:26.238
Was that among the items
that were sent to you?


01:43:27.139 --> 01:43:28.173
Yes, sir.


01:43:29.342 --> 01:43:30.542
And is that the ring


01:43:30.575 --> 01:43:33.011
that Emmett came down here
to Mississippi with?


01:43:34.012 --> 01:43:35.080
Yes, sir.


01:43:36.648 --> 01:43:40.685
Mamie, I wish
you would state to the court,


01:43:41.387 --> 01:43:42.754
and to the jury,


01:43:42.788 --> 01:43:45.090
whether you could identify
the body


01:43:45.123 --> 01:43:47.826
that you saw down there
in the funeral home


01:43:47.859 --> 01:43:50.128
as that of your son,
Emmett Till.


01:43:51.364 --> 01:43:52.632
I could.


01:43:59.473 --> 01:44:02.809
It's hard to describe
what a mother knows.


01:44:04.644 --> 01:44:05.878
Please.


01:44:12.185 --> 01:44:15.255
The first thing I noticed
when I became a mother


01:44:15.922 --> 01:44:18.358
was that my hands were busy.


01:44:18.392 --> 01:44:20.626
All the time.


01:44:20.660 --> 01:44:24.331
Rocking, carrying, swaying,
always full.


01:44:24.764 --> 01:44:26.433
One hand for him,


01:44:26.467 --> 01:44:28.668
and one hand for what he needed.


01:44:29.936 --> 01:44:32.071
When it came time
to place him down


01:44:32.105 --> 01:44:34.342
so he could make
his own way around,


01:44:35.477 --> 01:44:37.345
I touched every inch of him.


01:44:38.045 --> 01:44:40.114
Every bend.


01:44:40.147 --> 01:44:44.319
My hand knew him
with my eyes closed.


01:44:44.352 --> 01:44:45.619
Just like I'd know his laughter


01:44:45.652 --> 01:44:47.121
in a crowded room.


01:44:48.256 --> 01:44:52.059
It's the same thing
when you know all of someone.


01:45:04.771 --> 01:45:08.709
I started by laying my hands
on a foot.


01:45:10.378 --> 01:45:11.879
And then


01:45:13.046 --> 01:45:14.682
found his knees.


01:45:16.885 --> 01:45:18.987
I remembered him...


01:45:20.889 --> 01:45:24.893
as my fingers
traced his hairline,


01:45:26.127 --> 01:45:30.332
and bumped over the crease
of his eyelid.


01:45:32.667 --> 01:45:35.170
He was spoiled and puffed,


01:45:36.405 --> 01:45:37.839
but these were the same parts


01:45:37.872 --> 01:45:40.008
of a boy I'd nurtured and loved.


01:45:41.042 --> 01:45:43.912
Nothing and no one
could hide him from me.


01:45:46.181 --> 01:45:47.749
A mother knows.


01:45:49.217 --> 01:45:50.919
Your mother would know.


01:45:52.020 --> 01:45:52.854
And I knew.


01:45:52.887 --> 01:45:57.960
I knew this was my boy.
Emmett Till.


01:45:58.628 --> 01:46:00.263
Beyond any doubt.


01:46:03.032 --> 01:46:05.000
Thank you. Uh...


01:46:06.503 --> 01:46:08.938
Thank you, Mrs. Bradley.


01:46:08.971 --> 01:46:11.807
I believe that's all any of us
would ever need to hear.


01:46:16.413 --> 01:46:17.514
Mamie?


01:46:17.547 --> 01:46:18.582
Do you happen to remember


01:46:18.615 --> 01:46:20.584
the date
Emmett Till's father died?


01:46:20.617 --> 01:46:24.119
Yes, sir.
July the 2nd, 1945.


01:46:24.153 --> 01:46:25.622
Where was he when he died?


01:46:25.655 --> 01:46:26.989
In Europe.


01:46:28.090 --> 01:46:30.726
Did you have an insurance
policy on Emmett Till?


01:46:31.494 --> 01:46:32.662
Um...


01:46:32.696 --> 01:46:34.431
Yes, sir.


01:46:34.464 --> 01:46:36.601
How much was it for?


01:46:36.634 --> 01:46:39.869
I had a 10-cent
and 15-cent policy,


01:46:39.903 --> 01:46:43.006
two weekly policies,
and they equaled $400.


01:46:43.039 --> 01:46:45.108
$400?


01:46:46.611 --> 01:46:48.379
Now, to whom
were those policies payable?


01:46:48.412 --> 01:46:50.981
Uh,
we object to that, Your Honor.


01:46:51.014 --> 01:46:52.650
Objection overruled.


01:46:52.683 --> 01:46:54.851
The witness
will answer the question.


01:46:55.919 --> 01:46:57.988
I was the beneficiary on one,


01:46:58.021 --> 01:46:59.889
and my mother was on the other.


01:47:00.957 --> 01:47:01.992
He ever cause


01:47:02.025 --> 01:47:03.760
or get in any trouble
in Chicago?


01:47:04.595 --> 01:47:05.696
No more than any other boy.


01:47:05.730 --> 01:47:07.163
Did he attend a reform school?


01:47:07.197 --> 01:47:08.432
What for?


01:47:08.466 --> 01:47:09.467
No.


01:47:10.834 --> 01:47:13.136
You've been quoted
in the colored press,


01:47:13.169 --> 01:47:15.872
"I told him several times
before he left for Mississippi


01:47:15.905 --> 01:47:17.309
"that he should kneel
in the street


01:47:17.342 --> 01:47:18.644
"and beg for forgiveness


01:47:18.677 --> 01:47:20.479
"should he ever insult
a White person."


01:47:20.512 --> 01:47:22.614
Not those exact words.


01:47:22.648 --> 01:47:25.082
Did you caution
him not to insult White women?


01:47:25.116 --> 01:47:28.019
I referred to White people
in general.


01:47:28.052 --> 01:47:29.721
Did you caution your son


01:47:29.755 --> 01:47:31.164
how to conduct himself
and behave himself


01:47:31.188 --> 01:47:32.467
while he was down here
in Mississippi?


01:47:32.491 --> 01:47:33.425
Several times.


01:47:33.458 --> 01:47:35.993
Several times!
Do tell us how.


01:47:36.027 --> 01:47:37.928
I will give you
a literal description


01:47:37.962 --> 01:47:39.298
of what I told him.


01:47:39.331 --> 01:47:40.532
How coming down here,


01:47:40.565 --> 01:47:43.834
he would have to adapt himself
to a different way of life.


01:47:43.868 --> 01:47:45.936
Be very careful
about how he spoke,


01:47:45.970 --> 01:47:47.372
and to whom he spoke,


01:47:47.406 --> 01:47:51.075
and to always remember to say,
"Yes, sir" and "No, ma'am."


01:47:51.108 --> 01:47:53.578
I told him that if ever
an incident should arise


01:47:53.612 --> 01:47:54.945
where there would be any trouble


01:47:54.979 --> 01:47:56.448
of any kind with White people,


01:47:56.481 --> 01:47:58.584
that if it got to the point
where he needed


01:47:58.618 --> 01:48:00.386
to go down on his knees
before them,


01:48:00.420 --> 01:48:03.790
well, I told him
not to hesitate to do so.


01:48:03.822 --> 01:48:06.958
Like if he bumped
into somebody on the street


01:48:06.992 --> 01:48:09.262
and they might get belligerent
or something.


01:48:09.295 --> 01:48:12.097
Well, I told him to go ahead
and humble himself


01:48:12.130 --> 01:48:15.335
so as not to get into
any trouble! But...


01:48:16.402 --> 01:48:17.537
But what?


01:48:18.771 --> 01:48:22.275
Well, I raised him with love
for 14 years.


01:48:22.308 --> 01:48:26.244
My sudden warnings about hate
weren't going to get through.


01:48:27.447 --> 01:48:28.980
I now show you
what purports to be


01:48:29.014 --> 01:48:30.550
a photograph of your son.


01:48:33.286 --> 01:48:37.690
This was taken in my home
two days after Christmas.


01:48:37.724 --> 01:48:40.294
Now, tell the court
and the jury what this is.


01:48:42.262 --> 01:48:45.532
This picture is of my son


01:48:45.566 --> 01:48:49.570
after Mississippi sent him
back to Chicago, dead.


01:48:53.106 --> 01:48:54.508
No further questions.


01:48:56.276 --> 01:48:58.077
And for the prosecution?


01:48:59.713 --> 01:49:01.080
State rests.


01:49:03.384 --> 01:49:04.984
Court will have a recess.


01:49:10.890 --> 01:49:12.191
They...


01:49:12.225 --> 01:49:15.194
They killed my son again.


01:49:23.705 --> 01:49:25.005
Hmm.


01:50:06.114 --> 01:50:08.617
Will the jury please
retire to the jury room?


01:50:11.520 --> 01:50:14.390
The testimony
being offered here today


01:50:14.423 --> 01:50:17.526
of a prior incident
at the store in Money


01:50:17.560 --> 01:50:18.727
is irrelevant.


01:50:19.895 --> 01:50:21.062
Your Honor,


01:50:21.095 --> 01:50:23.833
may we still continue
the testimony


01:50:23.866 --> 01:50:26.034
on account of the record?


01:50:26.067 --> 01:50:27.503
Uh, Your Honor...


01:50:27.536 --> 01:50:29.037
Sit down.


01:50:29.971 --> 01:50:32.808
Now, I see no harm
in letting Ms. Bryant


01:50:32.842 --> 01:50:36.177
share her side of things
if she wants to.


01:50:36.211 --> 01:50:38.414
Hell, everybody else has.


01:50:38.447 --> 01:50:40.449
You think
you can handle that, dear?


01:50:48.825 --> 01:50:50.260
Mrs. Bryant,


01:50:51.060 --> 01:50:53.195
was anyone in the store with you


01:50:53.229 --> 01:50:57.701
on Wednesday night,
24th day of August, 1955?


01:50:59.936 --> 01:51:01.338
I was alone.


01:51:02.439 --> 01:51:05.007
But the children
were in the back.


01:51:05.040 --> 01:51:06.643
In the living quarters.


01:51:07.944 --> 01:51:10.347
And what time of day was it?


01:51:10.380 --> 01:51:11.581
After dark.


01:51:12.983 --> 01:51:14.016
Alone.


01:51:14.049 --> 01:51:16.252
At nighttime with your children.


01:51:16.286 --> 01:51:18.788
Well, you just tell the court
what happened next.


01:51:21.056 --> 01:51:23.793
This nigger man
came into the store


01:51:23.827 --> 01:51:26.162
and stood by the candy case.


01:51:26.931 --> 01:51:28.533
And you?


01:51:28.566 --> 01:51:31.167
I was behind the counter.


01:51:31.201 --> 01:51:34.005
I asked the man what he wanted.


01:51:34.037 --> 01:51:36.541
And then did you get him
the merchandise?


01:51:36.574 --> 01:51:37.575
Yes.


01:51:39.175 --> 01:51:42.013
And then what did you do?


01:51:42.045 --> 01:51:44.382
I held out my hand
for the money.


01:51:45.583 --> 01:51:47.250
Will you show the court


01:51:47.285 --> 01:51:48.753
how you held your hand out?


01:51:50.588 --> 01:51:51.622
Like this.


01:51:51.656 --> 01:51:54.090
And did he give you the money?


01:51:54.124 --> 01:51:56.260
No, he caught my hand.


01:51:57.261 --> 01:51:59.162
Will you show the court


01:51:59.195 --> 01:52:01.299
just how he grasped your hand?


01:52:05.136 --> 01:52:07.005
And was that a strong grip
or a light grip


01:52:07.039 --> 01:52:09.575
that he had
when he held your hand?


01:52:09.608 --> 01:52:10.943
A strong grip.


01:52:13.177 --> 01:52:15.681
Will you show
the court what you did?


01:52:15.714 --> 01:52:17.349
How did you get loose?


01:52:22.754 --> 01:52:25.624
I jerked it loose like this.


01:52:26.792 --> 01:52:31.095
Now, just what did he say
when he grabbed your hand?


01:52:32.831 --> 01:52:35.701
- "How about a date, baby?"
- Hmm.


01:52:36.902 --> 01:52:39.071
Now, you freed yourself.


01:52:39.103 --> 01:52:40.606
And what happened then?


01:52:44.910 --> 01:52:47.212
I turned to the back
of the store.


01:52:49.114 --> 01:52:51.216
And he went on his way?


01:52:53.353 --> 01:52:55.120
No.


01:52:55.153 --> 01:52:58.558
He came after me.


01:52:58.591 --> 01:53:01.561
He caught me down
by the cash register.


01:53:04.097 --> 01:53:08.534
Mrs. Bryant, can you
demonstrate for the court?


01:53:11.404 --> 01:53:12.271
Yes.


01:53:12.305 --> 01:53:13.606
All right, now.


01:53:21.514 --> 01:53:24.283
Grabbed your hands,
pinned them behind your back?


01:53:26.552 --> 01:53:27.855
Yes.


01:53:27.888 --> 01:53:30.858
His right hand
on your right hip?


01:53:32.326 --> 01:53:33.827
Here.


01:53:34.995 --> 01:53:36.563
Just what did he say?


01:53:38.565 --> 01:53:42.636
He said,
"You needn't be afraid of me.


01:53:42.670 --> 01:53:44.672
"I've been
with White women before."


01:53:45.639 --> 01:53:47.741
And what happened then?


01:53:47.775 --> 01:53:50.209
Then another nigger
came in the door...


01:53:52.112 --> 01:53:54.314
I'm ready to go.


01:53:54.348 --> 01:53:55.716
You want me to come and get you


01:53:55.749 --> 01:53:56.650
when they read a verdict?


01:53:56.684 --> 01:54:00.821
No. I'm ready
to leave Mississippi. Now.


01:54:00.854 --> 01:54:02.322
What about the verdict?


01:54:03.323 --> 01:54:05.259
I know what the verdict is.


01:54:08.028 --> 01:54:10.532
<i>After deliberating
for about an hour,</i>


01:54:10.565 --> 01:54:12.934
<i>the jury has just come back
with a verdict</i>


01:54:12.967 --> 01:54:14.936
<i>of "not guilty."</i>


01:54:14.969 --> 01:54:18.907
<i>Thus the defendants Milam
and Bryant are free men.</i>


01:54:18.940 --> 01:54:20.542
<i>They celebrated their victory</i>


01:54:20.575 --> 01:54:24.179
<i>laughing and smiling with
their wives at their side,</i>


01:54:24.211 --> 01:54:26.948
<i>clearly happy...</i>


01:55:00.248 --> 01:55:04.620
<i>Her story has changed the world.</i>


01:55:04.653 --> 01:55:08.357
<i>Because she had the courage
to make it not just her own,</i>


01:55:09.024 --> 01:55:10.326
<i>but all of ours.</i>


01:55:13.028 --> 01:55:16.665
<i>Mamie, it is an honor
to share the stage with you.</i>


01:55:18.334 --> 01:55:20.302
<i>To share this fight with you.</i>


01:55:20.336 --> 01:55:22.338
Yes, yes!


01:55:22.371 --> 01:55:27.610
<i>Please welcome
Mrs. Mamie Till-Bradley.</i>


01:55:32.649 --> 01:55:34.217
This is just the beginning.


01:55:43.860 --> 01:55:48.098
<i>I would like to
give honor to God,</i>


01:55:48.131 --> 01:55:50.167
<i>who is the source of my strength</i>


01:55:50.200 --> 01:55:52.068
<i>and the reason for my being.</i>


01:55:53.370 --> 01:55:56.873
<i>I thank you,
Mr. Mooty and the NAACP,</i>


01:55:56.907 --> 01:55:59.876
<i>for inviting me
to speak before you all</i>


01:55:59.910 --> 01:56:01.678
<i>in Harlem, New York City.</i>


01:56:02.078 --> 01:56:03.680
Yes.


01:56:03.713 --> 01:56:06.683
<i>My son's brutalized body
meant nothing</i>


01:56:06.716 --> 01:56:09.886
<i>to Mississippi's
criminal justice system.</i>


01:56:09.920 --> 01:56:13.124
<i>And while they blamed
the victim, as usual,</i>


01:56:13.157 --> 01:56:16.527
<i>the federal government
stood idly by.</i>


01:56:16.561 --> 01:56:19.096
<i>If this country fails to protect</i>


01:56:19.130 --> 01:56:20.765
<i>the Black body from hate,</i>


01:56:20.798 --> 01:56:23.234
<i>America has yet to meet
her promise.</i>


01:56:23.268 --> 01:56:24.535
Amen!


01:56:24.569 --> 01:56:28.072
<i>Either freedom for everyone,
or freedom fails!</i>


01:56:36.848 --> 01:56:40.918
<i>One month ago, I had
a nice apartment in Chicago.</i>


01:56:40.952 --> 01:56:45.556
<i>I had a good job. I had a son.</i>


01:56:45.590 --> 01:56:47.992
<i>When something happened
to the Negroes in the South,</i>


01:56:48.025 --> 01:56:52.029
<i>I said, "Well, that's
their business. Not mine."</i>


01:56:52.063 --> 01:56:55.601
<i>Now I know how wrong I was.</i>


01:56:55.634 --> 01:56:57.903
<i>The lynching of my son
has shown me</i>


01:56:57.936 --> 01:56:59.972
<i>that what happens to any of us,</i>


01:57:00.005 --> 01:57:01.274
<i>anywhere in the world,</i>


01:57:01.307 --> 01:57:04.376
<i>had better be the business
of us all.</i>


01:57:19.258 --> 01:57:20.893
I hear ya, sister!


01:57:21.426 --> 01:57:22.828
That's right.


01:57:23.595 --> 01:57:25.197
Tell it like it is!


01:57:25.230 --> 01:57:26.531
I heard that!


01:57:27.900 --> 01:57:29.434
Yes! Yes!

